    ('july-04', 'july-04-extra-order', 38, 'Use It', 'order', '{"id":"july-04-extra-order","format":"order","type":"order","section":"Use It","topic":"possibility","isOriginal":false,"hint":"Focus on the possibility meaning. Look for the sentence that expresses “あとで雨が降るかもしれません。”.","hintJa":"might は不確かな可能性。","explanation":"Correct order: “It might rain later.”. Keep the subject, verb and remaining information in that order.","explanationJa":"正しい語順は「It might rain later.」です。主語・動詞・残りの情報の順を確認しましょう。","prompt":"Put the words in order: あとで雨が降るかもしれません。","promptJa":"語順を並べましょう：あとで雨が降るかもしれません。","words":["later","rain","might","It"],"correctWords":["It","might","rain","later"]}'::jsonb, false, 1),
    ('july-04', 'july-04-extra-matching', 39, 'Use It', 'matching', '{"id":"july-04-extra-matching","format":"matching","type":"matching","section":"Use It","topic":"conversation","isOriginal":false,"hint":"Focus on the conversation meaning. Look for the sentence that expresses “実は今日は少し疲れています。”.","hintJa":"Actually で本当の情報を加える。","explanation":"Each English phrase has one Japanese partner with the same meaning. Recheck the complete phrase when two items share a similar word.","explanationJa":"各英文には、同じ意味の日本語が一つずつあります。似た単語がある時も、表現全体の意味で確認しましょう。","prompt":"Match each English phrase with its natural Japanese meaning.","promptJa":"英文と自然な日本語を組み合わせてください。","pairs":[{"en":"Actually, I’m a little tired today.","jp":"実は今日は少し疲れています。","cat":"conversation"},{"en":"I avoid driving when I’m tired.","jp":"疲れている時は運転を避けます。","cat":"safety"},{"en":"Something came up.","jp":"急な事情ができました。","cat":"unexpected events"},{"en":"It can’t be helped.","jp":"仕方ありません。","cat":"responses"},{"en":"He didn’t do it on purpose.","jp":"彼はわざとしたのではありません。","cat":"intention"},{"en":"I really appreciate it.","jp":"本当に感謝しています。","cat":"gratitude"}]}'::jsonb, false, 6),
    ('july-04', 'july-04-extra-sorting', 40, 'Use It', 'sorting', '{"id":"july-04-extra-sorting","format":"sorting","type":"sorting","section":"Use It","topic":"safety","isOriginal":false,"hint":"Focus on the safety meaning. Look for the sentence that expresses “疲れている時は運転を避けます。”.","hintJa":"avoid + 動詞-ing。","explanation":"The categories describe language purpose: conversation, safety. Sort by what each complete phrase does in conversation.","explanationJa":"分類は「conversation・safety」です。単語一つではなく、会話でその表現が果たす役割で分けましょう。","prompt":"Sort each phrase by its language purpose.","promptJa":"各表現を目的別に分類してください。","categories":["conversation","safety"],"items":[["Actually, I’m a little tired today.","conversation"],["I avoid driving when I’m tired.","safety"]]}'::jsonb, false, 2),
    ('july-04', 'july-04-extra-dialogue', 41, 'Use It', 'dialogue', '{"id":"july-04-extra-dialogue","format":"dialogue","type":"dialogue","section":"Use It","topic":"safety","isOriginal":false,"hint":"Focus on the safety meaning. Look for the sentence that expresses “疲れている時は運転を避けます。”.","hintJa":"avoid + 動詞-ing。","explanation":"“I avoid driving when I’m tired.” responds directly and naturally to the previous line.","explanationJa":"「I avoid driving when I’m tired.」は、直前の発言に直接答える自然な一文です。","prompt":"Choose the most natural next line in the conversation.","promptJa":"会話の次に続く最も自然な一文を選んでください。","context":"A: What do you do when you’re too tired to drive safely?\nB: ...","contextJa":"A：「疲れて安全に運転できない時はどうする？」\nB：…","choices":[{"id":"a","en":"I avoid driving when I’m tired.","jp":"疲れている時は運転を避けます。"},{"id":"b","en":"Something came up.","jp":"急な事情ができました。"},{"id":"c","en":"He didn’t do it on purpose.","jp":"彼はわざとしたのではありません。"},{"id":"d","en":"It might rain later.","jp":"あとで雨が降るかもしれません。"}],"correct":"a"}'::jsonb, false, 1),
    ('july-04', 'july-04-extra-translation', 42, 'Use It', 'translation', '{"id":"july-04-extra-translation","format":"translation","type":"translation","section":"Use It","topic":"unexpected events","isOriginal":false,"hint":"Focus on the unexpected events meaning. Look for the sentence that expresses “急な事情ができました。”.","hintJa":"予定変更の自然な説明。","explanation":"A natural translation is “Something came up.”. It expresses “急な事情ができました。” with the lesson’s unexpected events pattern.","explanationJa":"自然な英訳は「Something came up.」です。「急な事情ができました。」を今回のunexpected events表現で伝えています。","prompt":"Translate into English: 急な事情ができました。","promptJa":"英語にしてください：急な事情ができました。","accepted":["Something came up."]}'::jsonb, false, 1),
    ('july-04', 'july-04-extra-situation', 43, 'Use It', 'situation', '{"id":"july-04-extra-situation","format":"situation","type":"situation","section":"Use It","topic":"responses","isOriginal":false,"hint":"Focus on the responses meaning. Look for the sentence that expresses “仕方ありません。”.","hintJa":"変えられない状況への反応。","explanation":"“It can’t be helped.” directly expresses “仕方ありません。”. The other choices describe different situations.","explanationJa":"「It can’t be helped.」が「仕方ありません。」を直接表します。他の選択肢は別の場面を表しています。","prompt":"Which sentence best expresses this meaning: 仕方ありません。","promptJa":"「仕方ありません。」に最も合う英文はどれですか？","choices":[{"id":"a","en":"It can’t be helped.","jp":"仕方ありません。"},{"id":"b","en":"He didn’t do it on purpose.","jp":"彼はわざとしたのではありません。"},{"id":"c","en":"Don’t mention it.","jp":"どういたしまして。"},{"id":"d","en":"I avoid driving when I’m tired.","jp":"疲れている時は運転を避けます。"}],"correct":"a"}'::jsonb, false, 1),
    ('july-04', 'july-04-extra-visual-1', 44, 'See It', 'situation', '{"id":"july-04-extra-visual-1","format":"situation","type":"situation","section":"See It","topic":"safety","isOriginal":false,"hint":"Use the visible action and objects as evidence: A tired person leaves the car keys at home and chooses the train. Choose the sentence that describes the complete scene.","hintJa":"人物の動作や物を確認し、「疲れている時は運転を避けます。」に合う場面か考えましょう。見えている場面全体を説明する英文を選んでください。","explanation":"The illustration shows this scene: A tired person leaves the car keys at home and chooses the train. That directly matches “I avoid driving when I’m tired.” (疲れている時は運転を避けます。); the other choices describe different actions or situations.","explanationJa":"人物の動作や物が「疲れている時は運転を避けます。」という場面を表しています。そのため「I avoid driving when I’m tired.」が一致し、他の選択肢は別の動作・場面です。","prompt":"Which sentence best matches the illustration?","promptJa":"イラストの場面に最も合う英文を選んでください。","choices":[{"id":"a","en":"I avoid driving when I’m tired.","jp":"疲れている時は運転を避けます。"},{"id":"b","en":"Actually, I’m a little tired today.","jp":"実は今日は少し疲れています。"},{"id":"c","en":"Something came up.","jp":"急な事情ができました。"},{"id":"d","en":"It might rain later.","jp":"あとで雨が降るかもしれません。"}],"correct":"a","image":"/assets/questions/visual/july-04-01-avoid-driving-tired.webp","imageAlt":"A tired person leaves the car keys at home and chooses the train.","visualAssetId":"july-04-01"}'::jsonb, false, 1),
    ('july-04', 'july-04-extra-visual-2', 45, 'See It', 'situation', '{"id":"july-04-extra-visual-2","format":"situation","type":"situation","section":"See It","topic":"unexpected events","isOriginal":false,"hint":"Use the visible action and objects as evidence: An urgent phone call unexpectedly interrupts a planned appointment. Choose the sentence that describes the complete scene.","hintJa":"人物の動作や物を確認し、「急な事情ができました。」に合う場面か考えましょう。見えている場面全体を説明する英文を選んでください。","explanation":"The illustration shows this scene: An urgent phone call unexpectedly interrupts a planned appointment. That directly matches “Something came up.” (急な事情ができました。); the other choices describe different actions or situations.","explanationJa":"人物の動作や物が「急な事情ができました。」という場面を表しています。そのため「Something came up.」が一致し、他の選択肢は別の動作・場面です。","prompt":"Which sentence best matches the illustration?","promptJa":"イラストの場面に最も合う英文を選んでください。","choices":[{"id":"a","en":"Something came up.","jp":"急な事情ができました。"},{"id":"b","en":"Actually, I’m a little tired today.","jp":"実は今日は少し疲れています。"},{"id":"c","en":"It can’t be helped.","jp":"仕方ありません。"},{"id":"d","en":"I really appreciate it.","jp":"本当に感謝しています。"}],"correct":"a","image":"/assets/questions/visual/july-04-02-something-came-up.webp","imageAlt":"An urgent phone call unexpectedly interrupts a planned appointment.","visualAssetId":"july-04-02"}'::jsonb, false, 1),
    ('july-04', 'july-04-extra-visual-3', 46, 'See It', 'situation', '{"id":"july-04-extra-visual-3","format":"situation","type":"situation","section":"See It","topic":"intention","isOriginal":false,"hint":"Use the visible action and objects as evidence: A man accidentally bumps a table and apologizes for spilling a drink. Choose the sentence that describes the complete scene.","hintJa":"人物の動作や物を確認し、「彼はわざとしたのではありません。」に合う場面か考えましょう。見えている場面全体を説明する英文を選んでください。","explanation":"The illustration shows this scene: A man accidentally bumps a table and apologizes for spilling a drink. That directly matches “He didn’t do it on purpose.” (彼はわざとしたのではありません。); the other choices describe different actions or situations.","explanationJa":"人物の動作や物が「彼はわざとしたのではありません。」という場面を表しています。そのため「He didn’t do it on purpose.」が一致し、他の選択肢は別の動作・場面です。","prompt":"Which sentence best matches the illustration?","promptJa":"イラストの場面に最も合う英文を選んでください。","choices":[{"id":"a","en":"He didn’t do it on purpose.","jp":"彼はわざとしたのではありません。"},{"id":"b","en":"Something came up.","jp":"急な事情ができました。"},{"id":"c","en":"It can’t be helped.","jp":"仕方ありません。"},{"id":"d","en":"I really appreciate it.","jp":"本当に感謝しています。"}],"correct":"a","image":"/assets/questions/visual/july-04-03-not-on-purpose.webp","imageAlt":"A man accidentally bumps a table and apologizes for spilling a drink.","visualAssetId":"july-04-03"}'::jsonb, false, 1),
    ('july-04', 'july-04-extra-visual-4', 47, 'See It', 'situation', '{"id":"july-04-extra-visual-4","format":"situation","type":"situation","section":"See It","topic":"gratitude","isOriginal":false,"hint":"Use the visible action and objects as evidence: A grateful person sincerely thanks someone who helped carry heavy boxes. Choose the sentence that describes the complete scene.","hintJa":"人物の動作や物を確認し、「本当に感謝しています。」に合う場面か考えましょう。見えている場面全体を説明する英文を選んでください。","explanation":"The illustration shows this scene: A grateful person sincerely thanks someone who helped carry heavy boxes. That directly matches “I really appreciate it.” (本当に感謝しています。); the other choices describe different actions or situations.","explanationJa":"人物の動作や物が「本当に感謝しています。」という場面を表しています。そのため「I really appreciate it.」が一致し、他の選択肢は別の動作・場面です。","prompt":"Which sentence best matches the illustration?","promptJa":"イラストの場面に最も合う英文を選んでください。","choices":[{"id":"a","en":"I really appreciate it.","jp":"本当に感謝しています。"},{"id":"b","en":"Actually, I’m a little tired today.","jp":"実は今日は少し疲れています。"},{"id":"c","en":"It can’t be helped.","jp":"仕方ありません。"},{"id":"d","en":"Don’t mention it.","jp":"どういたしまして。"}],"correct":"a","image":"/assets/questions/visual/july-04-04-appreciate-help.webp","imageAlt":"A grateful person sincerely thanks someone who helped carry heavy boxes.","visualAssetId":"july-04-04"}'::jsonb, false, 1),
    ('july-04', 'july-04-extra-visual-5', 48, 'See It', 'situation', '{"id":"july-04-extra-visual-5","format":"situation","type":"situation","section":"See It","topic":"possibility","isOriginal":false,"hint":"Use the visible action and objects as evidence: A person notices dark clouds and carries an umbrella because it might rain later. Choose the sentence that describes the complete scene.","hintJa":"人物の動作や物を確認し、「あとで雨が降るかもしれません。」に合う場面か考えましょう。見えている場面全体を説明する英文を選んでください。","explanation":"The illustration shows this scene: A person notices dark clouds and carries an umbrella because it might rain later. That directly matches “It might rain later.” (あとで雨が降るかもしれません。); the other choices describe different actions or situations.","explanationJa":"人物の動作や物が「あとで雨が降るかもしれません。」という場面を表しています。そのため「It might rain later.」が一致し、他の選択肢は別の動作・場面です。","prompt":"Which sentence best matches the illustration?","promptJa":"イラストの場面に最も合う英文を選んでください。","choices":[{"id":"a","en":"It might rain later.","jp":"あとで雨が降るかもしれません。"},{"id":"b","en":"Actually, I’m a little tired today.","jp":"実は今日は少し疲れています。"},{"id":"c","en":"I avoid driving when I’m tired.","jp":"疲れている時は運転を避けます。"},{"id":"d","en":"I really appreciate it.","jp":"本当に感謝しています。"}],"correct":"a","image":"/assets/questions/visual/july-04-05-might-rain.webp","imageAlt":"A person notices dark clouds and carries an umbrella because it might rain later.","visualAssetId":"july-04-05"}'::jsonb, false, 1),
    ('july-05', 'july-05-original-q1', 0, 'Original Review', 'situation', '{"id":"july-05-original-q1","type":"situation","cat":"though","situationQuote":{"en":"A: This coffee is a little expensive."},"prompt":{"en":"You want to say 「まあ、美味しいけどね」. Which sentence is natural?","jp":"「まあ、美味しいけどね」と言いたい時、自然なのはどれですか？"},"choices":[{"id":"a","en":"It tastes good, though.","jp":"まあ、美味しいけどね。"},{"id":"b","en":"It tastes good, thought.","jp":"thought は「思った」の意味で違います。"},{"id":"c","en":"It though tastes good.","jp":"語順が不自然です。"},{"id":"d","en":"It tastes though good.","jp":"語順が不自然です。"}],"correct":"a","hint":{"en":"Put though at the end for 「〜だけどね」.","jp":"「〜だけどね」は文の最後に though を置きます。"},"explanation":{"en":"Sentence-final “though” softens the sentence and adds a natural “but still...” feeling.","jp":"文末の “though” は文をやわらかくして、「まあ〜だけどね」という自然な感じを出します。"},"legacyId":"q1","section":"Original Review","isOriginal":true}'::jsonb, true, 1),
    ('july-05', 'july-05-original-q2', 1, 'Original Review', 'mcq', '{"id":"july-05-original-q2","type":"mcq","cat":"though","prompt":{"en":"Which Japanese feeling is closest to “It’s expensive, though”?","jp":"“It’s expensive, though.” に一番近い日本語の感じはどれですか？"},"choices":[{"id":"a","en":"高いけどね。","jp":"自然です。"},{"id":"b","en":"高くないです。","jp":"意味が違います。"},{"id":"c","en":"高いと思いました。","jp":"thought の意味に近くなります。"},{"id":"d","en":"高くしてください。","jp":"意味が違います。"}],"correct":"a","hint":{"en":"though at the end often feels like 「だけどね」.","jp":"文末の though は「だけどね」に近いです。"},"explanation":{"en":"“It’s expensive, though” means the speaker admits it is expensive, but says it softly.","jp":"“It’s expensive, though.” は「高いけどね」と、少しやわらかく言っています。"},"legacyId":"q2","section":"Original Review","isOriginal":true}'::jsonb, true, 1),
    ('july-05', 'july-05-original-q3', 2, 'Original Review', 'mcq', '{"id":"july-05-original-q3","type":"mcq","cat":"though","prompt":{"en":"True or False: In casual conversation, “sentence + though” can mean 「〜だけどね」.","jp":"True or False：会話で “文 + though” は「〜だけどね」の感じになります。"},"choices":[{"id":"a","en":"True","jp":"正しい"},{"id":"b","en":"False","jp":"違う"}],"correct":"a","hint":{"en":"Example: I’m tired, though.","jp":"例：I’m tired, though. = 疲れてるけどね。"},"explanation":{"en":"True. This is a very useful casual pattern for soft reactions.","jp":"True です。やわらかく反応する時にとても便利な形です。"},"legacyId":"q3","section":"Original Review","isOriginal":true}'::jsonb, true, 1),
    ('july-05', 'july-05-original-q4', 3, 'Original Review', 'situation', '{"id":"july-05-original-q4","type":"situation","cat":"though","situationQuote":{"en":"Someone says, “You look busy.” But you are doing nothing special."},"prompt":{"en":"Choose the best reply.","jp":"一番自然な返事を選んでください。"},"choices":[{"id":"a","en":"I’m just sitting here, though.","jp":"ただ座ってるだけだけどね。"},{"id":"b","en":"I just sitting here, though.","jp":"be 動詞がないので不自然です。"},{"id":"c","en":"I’m just sit here, though.","jp":"動詞の形が不自然です。"},{"id":"d","en":"I’m just sitting here, thought.","jp":"thought ではありません。"}],"correct":"a","hint":{"en":"Use present continuous: I’m sitting.","jp":"今していることなので I’m sitting を使います。"},"explanation":{"en":"“I’m just sitting here, though” is natural when you softly correct someone’s impression.","jp":"“I’m just sitting here, though.” は、相手の印象をやわらかく訂正する時に自然です。"},"legacyId":"q4","section":"Original Review","isOriginal":true}'::jsonb, true, 1),
    ('july-05', 'july-05-original-q5', 4, 'Original Review', 'situation', '{"id":"july-05-original-q5","type":"situation","cat":"replies","situationQuote":{"en":"A: Thanks for waiting."},"prompt":{"en":"Which reply is casual and natural?","jp":"カジュアルで自然な返事はどれですか？"},"choices":[{"id":"a","en":"No problem.","jp":"全然大丈夫。"},{"id":"b","en":"Problem yes.","jp":"不自然です。"},{"id":"c","en":"Don’t worry?","jp":"疑問文になっていて不自然です。"},{"id":"d","en":"For here, please.","jp":"店内でお願いします、なので場面が違います。"}],"correct":"a","hint":{"en":"This means it was not a problem for you.","jp":"「迷惑じゃなかったよ」という感じです。"},"explanation":{"en":"“No problem” is common when someone thanks you for a small favor.","jp":"“No problem.” は軽い手伝いに対する「全然大丈夫」として自然です。"},"legacyId":"q5","section":"Original Review","isOriginal":true}'::jsonb, true, 1),
    ('july-05', 'july-05-original-q6', 5, 'Original Review', 'situation', '{"id":"july-05-original-q6","type":"situation","cat":"replies","situationQuote":{"en":"A: Thank you, and sorry for the trouble."},"prompt":{"en":"Which reply sounds kind and reassuring?","jp":"優しく安心させる返事はどれですか？"},"choices":[{"id":"a","en":"No worries. It’s totally fine.","jp":"気にしないで。全然大丈夫だよ。"},{"id":"b","en":"It’s expensive, though.","jp":"高いけどね、なので場面が違います。"},{"id":"c","en":"This is my go-to coffee.","jp":"定番コーヒーの話なので違います。"},{"id":"d","en":"Takeaway available?","jp":"持ち帰りできますか、なので違います。"}],"correct":"a","hint":{"en":"Use this when the other person feels sorry.","jp":"相手が申し訳なさそうな時に使いやすいです。"},"explanation":{"en":"“No worries” sounds warm and gentle, especially when someone apologizes while thanking you.","jp":"“No worries.” は、相手が謝りながら感謝している時に優しく聞こえます。"},"legacyId":"q6","section":"Original Review","isOriginal":true}'::jsonb, true, 1),
    ('july-05', 'july-05-original-q7', 6, 'Original Review', 'mcq', '{"id":"july-05-original-q7","type":"mcq","cat":"replies","prompt":{"en":"Which reply sounds polite and a little elegant, often used in service or business?","jp":"接客・ビジネスでも使える丁寧で上品な返事はどれですか？"},"choices":[{"id":"a","en":"My pleasure.","jp":"喜んで / お役に立てて嬉しいです。"},{"id":"b","en":"My problem.","jp":"不自然です。"},{"id":"c","en":"My takeaway.","jp":"意味が違います。"},{"id":"d","en":"My though.","jp":"意味が違います。"}],"correct":"a","hint":{"en":"Pleasure = 喜び.","jp":"pleasure は「喜び」です。"},"explanation":{"en":"“My pleasure” is polite and refined. It means you were happy to help.","jp":"“My pleasure.” は丁寧で上品な返事です。「喜んで / お役に立てて嬉しいです」という感じです。"},"legacyId":"q7","section":"Original Review","isOriginal":true}'::jsonb, true, 1),
    ('july-05', 'july-05-original-q8', 7, 'Original Review', 'mcq', '{"id":"july-05-original-q8","type":"mcq","cat":"replies","prompt":{"en":"Mistake Detective: Which reply means 「またいつでも言って」?","jp":"ミス発見：「またいつでも言って」に近い返事はどれですか？"},"choices":[{"id":"a","en":"Anytime.","jp":"いつでも言って。"},{"id":"b","en":"Always.","jp":"いつも、という意味で返事としては違います。"},{"id":"c","en":"To go.","jp":"持ち帰りで、なので違います。"},{"id":"d","en":"Though.","jp":"だけどね、なので違います。"}],"correct":"a","hint":{"en":"It means you are happy to help again.","jp":"また助けてもいいよ、という感じです。"},"explanation":{"en":"“Anytime” is natural when you want to say the person can ask you again.","jp":"“Anytime.” は「またいつでも言って」という自然な返事です。"},"legacyId":"q8","section":"Original Review","isOriginal":true}'::jsonb, true, 1),
    ('july-05', 'july-05-original-q9', 8, 'Original Review', 'matching', '{"id":"july-05-original-q9","type":"matching","cat":"mixed","prompt":{"en":"Speed Match: Match each reply with the Japanese feeling.","jp":"スピードマッチ：英語の返事と日本語の感じを合わせましょう。"},"hint":{"en":"Think about the feeling, not only the dictionary meaning.","jp":"単語の意味だけではなく、雰囲気で考えましょう。"},"pairs":[{"en":"You’re welcome.","jp":"どういたしまして。","cat":"replies"},{"en":"No problem.","jp":"全然大丈夫。","cat":"replies"},{"en":"No worries.","jp":"気にしないで。","cat":"replies"},{"en":"Of course.","jp":"もちろん。","cat":"replies"},{"en":"Anytime.","jp":"いつでも言って。","cat":"replies"},{"en":"My pleasure.","jp":"喜んで。","cat":"replies"},{"en":"Don’t mention it.","jp":"お礼なんていいよ。","cat":"replies"}],"explanation":{"en":"There are 7 one-to-one pairs. Match each complete English expression with the Japanese text that has the same meaning; similar-looking words are not enough.","jp":"7組を一対一で合わせます。似た単語だけで判断せず、英文全体と同じ意味の日本語を選びましょう。"},"legacyId":"q9","section":"Original Review","isOriginal":true}'::jsonb, true, 7),
    ('july-05', 'july-05-original-q10', 9, 'Original Review', 'situation', '{"id":"july-05-original-q10","type":"situation","cat":"takeout","situationQuote":{"en":"You are ordering coffee at a café. You want to take it home."},"prompt":{"en":"What is the shortest natural answer?","jp":"一番短く自然な答えはどれですか？"},"choices":[{"id":"a","en":"To go, please.","jp":"持ち帰りでお願いします。"},{"id":"b","en":"Go to, please.","jp":"go to では意味が違います。"},{"id":"c","en":"For here, please.","jp":"店内でお願いします、なので逆です。"},{"id":"d","en":"Though, please.","jp":"不自然です。"}],"correct":"a","hint":{"en":"In the U.S., “to go” is very natural at cafés.","jp":"アメリカではカフェで “to go” がとても自然です。"},"explanation":{"en":"“To go, please” is a simple natural way to say 持ち帰りでお願いします.","jp":"“To go, please.” は「持ち帰りでお願いします」の短く自然な言い方です。"},"legacyId":"q10","section":"Original Review","isOriginal":true}'::jsonb, true, 1),
    ('july-05', 'july-05-original-q11', 10, 'Original Review', 'mcq', '{"id":"july-05-original-q11","type":"mcq","cat":"takeout","prompt":{"en":"Which question means 「店内ですか？お持ち帰りですか？」","jp":"「店内ですか？お持ち帰りですか？」はどれですか？"},"choices":[{"id":"a","en":"For here or to go?","jp":"店内ですか？お持ち帰りですか？"},{"id":"b","en":"For go or to here?","jp":"語順が不自然です。"},{"id":"c","en":"Here to for go?","jp":"文として不自然です。"},{"id":"d","en":"Takeout or coffee?","jp":"意味が違います。"}],"correct":"a","hint":{"en":"For here = 店内で. To go = 持ち帰りで.","jp":"For here = 店内で。To go = 持ち帰りで。"},"explanation":{"en":"Cashiers often ask “For here or to go?”","jp":"店員さんはよく “For here or to go?” と聞きます。"},"legacyId":"q11","section":"Original Review","isOriginal":true}'::jsonb, true, 1),
    ('july-05', 'july-05-original-q12', 11, 'Original Review', 'mcq', '{"id":"july-05-original-q12","type":"mcq","cat":"takeout","prompt":{"en":"True or False: “takeaway” is especially common in British/Australian English.","jp":"True or False：“takeaway” は特にイギリス・オーストラリア英語でよく使われます。"},"choices":[{"id":"a","en":"True","jp":"正しい"},{"id":"b","en":"False","jp":"違う"}],"correct":"a","hint":{"en":"takeout = often American. takeaway = often British/Australian.","jp":"takeout は米英語寄り、takeaway は英英語・豪英語寄りです。"},"explanation":{"en":"True. “takeaway” is common in British and Australian English.","jp":"True です。“takeaway” はイギリス英語・オーストラリア英語でよく使われます。"},"legacyId":"q12","section":"Original Review","isOriginal":true}'::jsonb, true, 1),
    ('july-05', 'july-05-original-q13', 12, 'Original Review', 'situation', '{"id":"july-05-original-q13","type":"situation","cat":"takeout","situationQuote":{"en":"A cashier asks: “For here or to go?” You want to eat inside."},"prompt":{"en":"Which answer is correct?","jp":"店内で食べたい時、正しい答えはどれですか？"},"choices":[{"id":"a","en":"For here, please.","jp":"店内でお願いします。"},{"id":"b","en":"To go, please.","jp":"持ち帰りでお願いします、なので逆です。"},{"id":"c","en":"Takeaway, please.","jp":"持ち帰りで、なので逆です。"},{"id":"d","en":"Go-to, please.","jp":"定番、なので違います。"}],"correct":"a","hint":{"en":"Here = inside the shop.","jp":"here は店内を指します。"},"explanation":{"en":"“For here, please” means you want to eat or drink inside.","jp":"“For here, please.” は「店内でお願いします」という意味です。"},"legacyId":"q13","section":"Original Review","isOriginal":true}'::jsonb, true, 1),
    ('july-05', 'july-05-original-q14', 13, 'Original Review', 'mcq', '{"id":"july-05-original-q14","type":"mcq","cat":"goto","prompt":{"en":"Which phrase means 「定番の / いつもの / 迷ったらこれ」?","jp":"「定番の / いつもの / 迷ったらこれ」はどれですか？"},"choices":[{"id":"a","en":"go-to","jp":"定番の / いつもの"},{"id":"b","en":"got to","jp":"〜しなければならない / 到着した、など別の意味です。"},{"id":"c","en":"to go","jp":"持ち帰りで、という意味です。"},{"id":"d","en":"though","jp":"だけどね、という意味です。"}],"correct":"a","hint":{"en":"The hyphen matters: go-to.","jp":"ハイフンが大事です：go-to。"},"explanation":{"en":"“go-to” means your usual reliable choice, like “my go-to coffee.”","jp":"“go-to” は「いつもの頼れる選択肢・定番」という意味です。"},"legacyId":"q14","section":"Original Review","isOriginal":true}'::jsonb, true, 1),
    ('july-05', 'july-05-original-q15', 14, 'Original Review', 'mcq', '{"id":"july-05-original-q15","type":"mcq","cat":"goto","prompt":{"en":"Mistake Detective: Which sentence is unnatural for 「これは私の定番コーヒーです」?","jp":"ミス発見：「これは私の定番コーヒーです」で不自然なのはどれですか？"},"choices":[{"id":"a","en":"This is my got to coffee.","jp":"got to では不自然です。"},{"id":"b","en":"This is my go-to coffee.","jp":"自然です。"},{"id":"c","en":"This coffee is my go-to.","jp":"自然です。"},{"id":"d","en":"This is my usual coffee.","jp":"自然です。"}],"correct":"a","hint":{"en":"go-to and got to are different.","jp":"go-to と got to は違います。"},"explanation":{"en":"Say “go-to coffee,” not “got to coffee.” “got to” has a different meaning.","jp":"“got to coffee” ではなく “go-to coffee” です。“got to” は別の意味です。"},"legacyId":"q15","section":"Original Review","isOriginal":true}'::jsonb, true, 1),
    ('july-05', 'july-05-original-q16', 15, 'Original Review', 'mcq', '{"id":"july-05-original-q16","type":"mcq","cat":"goto","prompt":{"en":"Which sentence uses “got to” correctly?","jp":"“got to” を正しく使っている文はどれですか？"},"choices":[{"id":"a","en":"I’ve got to go.","jp":"行かなきゃ。"},{"id":"b","en":"This is my got to coffee.","jp":"定番コーヒーには使いません。"},{"id":"c","en":"My got to restaurant is here.","jp":"定番レストランには go-to を使います。"},{"id":"d","en":"That’s my got to phrase.","jp":"定番フレーズには go-to を使います。"}],"correct":"a","hint":{"en":"“I’ve got to” is a common conversational form of “I have to.”","jp":"“I’ve got to” は会話で「〜しなければならない」を表します。"},"explanation":{"en":"“I’ve got to go” means “I have to go.” This is different from “go-to.”","jp":"“I’ve got to go.” は「行かなきゃ」という意味です。“go-to” とは別です。"},"legacyId":"q16","section":"Original Review","isOriginal":true}'::jsonb, true, 1),
    ('july-05', 'july-05-original-q17', 16, 'Original Review', 'order', '{"id":"july-05-original-q17","type":"order","cat":"builder","prompt":{"en":"Sentence Builder: Make 「まあ、美味しいけどね。」","jp":"文を組み立てましょう：「まあ、美味しいけどね。」"},"words":["though","good,","It","tastes"],"correctOrder":[2,3,1,0],"hint":{"en":"Put though at the end.","jp":"though は最後に置きます。"},"explanation":{"en":"The natural sentence is “It tastes good, though.”","jp":"自然な文は “It tastes good, though.” です。"},"legacyId":"q17","section":"Original Review","isOriginal":true}'::jsonb, true, 1),
    ('july-05', 'july-05-original-q18', 17, 'Original Review', 'order', '{"id":"july-05-original-q18","type":"order","cat":"builder","prompt":{"en":"Sentence Builder: Make 「これ持ち帰りでお願いします。」","jp":"文を組み立てましょう：「これ持ち帰りでお願いします。」"},"words":["get","Can","to go","this","I"],"correctOrder":[1,4,0,3,2],"hint":{"en":"Start with “Can I...”","jp":"“Can I...” から始めます。"},"explanation":{"en":"The natural sentence is “Can I get this to go?”","jp":"自然な文は “Can I get this to go?” です。"},"legacyId":"q18","section":"Original Review","isOriginal":true}'::jsonb, true, 1),
    ('july-05', 'july-05-original-q19', 18, 'Original Review', 'order', '{"id":"july-05-original-q19","type":"order","cat":"builder","prompt":{"en":"Sentence Builder: Make 「これは私の定番コーヒーです。」","jp":"文を組み立てましょう：「これは私の定番コーヒーです。」"},"words":["go-to","This","coffee","is","my"],"correctOrder":[1,3,4,0,2],"hint":{"en":"Use go-to, not got to.","jp":"got to ではなく go-to を使います。"},"explanation":{"en":"The natural sentence is “This is my go-to coffee.”","jp":"自然な文は “This is my go-to coffee.” です。"},"legacyId":"q19","section":"Original Review","isOriginal":true}'::jsonb, true, 1),
    ('july-05', 'july-05-original-q20', 19, 'Original Review', 'typing', '{"id":"july-05-original-q20","type":"typing","cat":"though","promptJP":"「ただ座ってるだけだけどね。」","accepted":["I''m just sitting here though","I am just sitting here though","I''m just sitting here, though","I am just sitting here, though"],"hint":{"en":"Use “I’m just sitting here” + though.","jp":"“I’m just sitting here” + though を使います。"},"explanation":{"en":"“I’m just sitting here, though” is a natural soft reply.","jp":"“I’m just sitting here, though.” は自然でやわらかい返事です。"},"prompt":{"en":"Write this meaning in natural English: 「ただ座ってるだけだけどね。」","jp":"次の意味を自然な英語にしてください：「ただ座ってるだけだけどね。」"},"legacyId":"q20","section":"Original Review","isOriginal":true}'::jsonb, true, 1),
    ('july-05', 'july-05-original-q21', 20, 'Original Review', 'typing', '{"id":"july-05-original-q21","type":"typing","cat":"replies","promptJP":"「全然大丈夫。」","accepted":["No problem","No worries"],"hint":{"en":"A short reply to thank you.","jp":"Thank you への短い返事です。"},"explanation":{"en":"“No problem” is very common. “No worries” also works kindly.","jp":"“No problem.” はとてもよく使います。“No worries.” も優しく自然です。"},"prompt":{"en":"Write this meaning in natural English: 「全然大丈夫。」","jp":"次の意味を自然な英語にしてください：「全然大丈夫。」"},"legacyId":"q21","section":"Original Review","isOriginal":true}'::jsonb, true, 1),
    ('july-05', 'july-05-original-q22', 21, 'Original Review', 'typing', '{"id":"july-05-original-q22","type":"typing","cat":"takeout","promptJP":"「持ち帰りでお願いします。」","accepted":["To go please","To go, please","Can I get this to go","Can I get it to go","Can I have this to go"],"hint":{"en":"At a café, the shortest answer is “To go, please.”","jp":"カフェでは “To go, please.” が短く自然です。"},"explanation":{"en":"“To go, please” and “Can I get this to go?” are both natural.","jp":"“To go, please.” と “Can I get this to go?” はどちらも自然です。"},"prompt":{"en":"Write this meaning in natural English: 「持ち帰りでお願いします。」","jp":"次の意味を自然な英語にしてください：「持ち帰りでお願いします。」"},"legacyId":"q22","section":"Original Review","isOriginal":true}'::jsonb, true, 1),
    ('july-05', 'july-05-original-q23', 22, 'Original Review', 'typing', '{"id":"july-05-original-q23","type":"typing","cat":"takeout","promptJP":"「店内ですか？お持ち帰りですか？」","accepted":["For here or to go","Is it for here or to go","For here or to go please"],"hint":{"en":"Cashiers often say this.","jp":"店員さんがよく言う表現です。"},"explanation":{"en":"“For here or to go?” is the standard café/restaurant question.","jp":"“For here or to go?” はカフェやレストランでよく聞く質問です。"},"prompt":{"en":"Write this meaning in natural English: 「店内ですか？お持ち帰りですか？」","jp":"次の意味を自然な英語にしてください：「店内ですか？お持ち帰りですか？」"},"legacyId":"q23","section":"Original Review","isOriginal":true}'::jsonb, true, 1),
    ('july-05', 'july-05-original-q24', 23, 'Original Review', 'typing', '{"id":"july-05-original-q24","type":"typing","cat":"goto","promptJP":"「これは私の定番コーヒーです。」","accepted":["This is my go-to coffee","This is my go to coffee","This coffee is my go-to","This coffee is my go to"],"hint":{"en":"Use go-to for 定番.","jp":"定番には go-to を使います。"},"explanation":{"en":"“This is my go-to coffee” means this is the coffee you usually choose.","jp":"“This is my go-to coffee.” は「いつも選ぶ定番コーヒー」という意味です。"},"prompt":{"en":"Write this meaning in natural English: 「これは私の定番コーヒーです。」","jp":"次の意味を自然な英語にしてください：「これは私の定番コーヒーです。」"},"legacyId":"q24","section":"Original Review","isOriginal":true}'::jsonb, true, 1),
    ('july-05', 'july-05-extra-listen-choice-1', 24, 'Listen & Speak', 'listenChoice', '{"id":"july-05-extra-listen-choice-1","format":"listenChoice","type":"listenChoice","section":"Listen & Speak","topic":"reactions","isOriginal":false,"hint":"Focus on the reactions meaning. Look for the sentence that expresses “なるほど、筋が通っています。”.","hintJa":"説明に納得した時。","explanation":"The sentence in the audio is “That makes sense.”. Listen for the complete phrase, not just one familiar word.","explanationJa":"音声の英文は「That makes sense.」です。知っている単語一つだけでなく、文全体を聞き取りましょう。","prompt":"Listen and choose the sentence you hear.","promptJa":"音声を聞いて、聞こえた英文を選んでください。","audioText":"That makes sense.","choices":[{"id":"a","en":"That makes sense.","jp":"なるほど、筋が通っています。"},{"id":"b","en":"I’d rather stay home tonight.","jp":"今夜は家にいたいです。"},{"id":"c","en":"I’m not sure yet.","jp":"まだ分かりません。"},{"id":"d","en":"I changed my mind.","jp":"考えが変わりました。"}],"correct":"a"}'::jsonb, false, 1),
    ('july-05', 'july-05-extra-listen-choice-2', 25, 'Listen & Speak', 'listenChoice', '{"id":"july-05-extra-listen-choice-2","format":"listenChoice","type":"listenChoice","section":"Listen & Speak","topic":"preferences","isOriginal":false,"hint":"Focus on the preferences meaning. Look for the sentence that expresses “今夜は家にいたいです。”.","hintJa":"would rather + 動詞原形。","explanation":"The sentence in the audio is “I’d rather stay home tonight.”. Listen for the complete phrase, not just one familiar word.","explanationJa":"音声の英文は「I’d rather stay home tonight.」です。知っている単語一つだけでなく、文全体を聞き取りましょう。","prompt":"Listen and choose the sentence you hear.","promptJa":"音声を聞いて、聞こえた英文を選んでください。","audioText":"I’d rather stay home tonight.","choices":[{"id":"a","en":"I’d rather stay home tonight.","jp":"今夜は家にいたいです。"},{"id":"b","en":"It depends on the weather.","jp":"天気によります。"},{"id":"c","en":"Let me think about it.","jp":"少し考えさせてください。"},{"id":"d","en":"Either option works for me.","jp":"どちらの選択肢でも大丈夫です。"}],"correct":"a"}'::jsonb, false, 1),
    ('july-05', 'july-05-extra-dictation-1', 26, 'Listen & Speak', 'listenType', '{"id":"july-05-extra-dictation-1","format":"listenType","type":"listenType","section":"Listen & Speak","topic":"decisions","isOriginal":false,"hint":"Focus on the decisions meaning. Look for the sentence that expresses “天気によります。”.","hintJa":"It depends on...","explanation":"The complete sentence is “It depends on the weather.”. Compare articles, auxiliaries and verb endings when you check your answer.","explanationJa":"全文は「It depends on the weather.」です。答え合わせでは冠詞・助動詞・動詞の語尾まで確認しましょう。","prompt":"Type the complete sentence you hear.","promptJa":"聞こえた英文をそのまま入力してください。","audioText":"It depends on the weather.","accepted":["It depends on the weather."]}'::jsonb, false, 1),
