    ('june-30', 'june-30-extra-speaking-5', 31, 'Listen & Speak', 'speaking', '{"id":"june-30-extra-speaking-5","format":"speaking","type":"speaking","section":"Listen & Speak","topic":"feelings","isOriginal":false,"hint":"Focus on the feelings meaning. Look for the sentence that expresses “何もうまくいかず、もどかしかったです。”.","hintJa":"frustrated は思い通りにならない気持ち。","explanation":"Model: “I was frustrated because nothing worked.” (何もうまくいかず、もどかしかったです。). Connect the complete message naturally; the second attempt checks independent recall.","explanationJa":"お手本は「I was frustrated because nothing worked.」（何もうまくいかず、もどかしかったです。）です。文全体を自然につなげ、2回目は見ずに思い出して言いましょう。","prompt":"Say the sentence naturally, then try once more without looking.","promptJa":"自然に言ってから、英文を見ずにもう一度話してみましょう。","speakText":"I was frustrated because nothing worked.","speakJa":"何もうまくいかず、もどかしかったです。"}'::jsonb, false, 1),
    ('june-30', 'june-30-extra-true-false', 32, 'Use It', 'truefalse', '{"id":"june-30-extra-true-false","format":"truefalse","type":"truefalse","section":"Use It","topic":"sports","isOriginal":false,"hint":"Focus on the sports meaning. Look for the sentence that expresses “後半はわくわくしました。”.","hintJa":"second half = 後半。","explanation":"True. “The second half was exciting.” means “後半はわくわくしました。”.","explanationJa":"正解はTrueです。「The second half was exciting.」は「後半はわくわくしました。」という意味です。","prompt":"“The second half was exciting.” means “後半はわくわくしました。”.","promptJa":"「The second half was exciting.」は「後半はわくわくしました。」という意味です。","correct":true}'::jsonb, false, 1),
    ('june-30', 'june-30-extra-order', 33, 'Use It', 'order', '{"id":"june-30-extra-order","format":"order","type":"order","section":"Use It","topic":"feelings","isOriginal":false,"hint":"Focus on the feelings meaning. Look for the sentence that expresses “何もうまくいかず、もどかしかったです。”.","hintJa":"frustrated は思い通りにならない気持ち。","explanation":"Correct order: “I was frustrated because nothing worked.”. Keep the subject, verb and remaining information in that order.","explanationJa":"正しい語順は「I was frustrated because nothing worked.」です。主語・動詞・残りの情報の順を確認しましょう。","prompt":"Put the words in order: 何もうまくいかず、もどかしかったです。","promptJa":"語順を並べましょう：何もうまくいかず、もどかしかったです。","words":["because","nothing","worked","I","was","frustrated"],"correctWords":["I","was","frustrated","because","nothing","worked"]}'::jsonb, false, 1),
    ('june-30', 'june-30-extra-matching', 34, 'Use It', 'matching', '{"id":"june-30-extra-matching","format":"matching","type":"matching","section":"Use It","topic":"feelings","isOriginal":false,"hint":"Focus on the feelings meaning. Look for the sentence that expresses “その音にイライラしています。”.","hintJa":"-ed は人の気持ち。","explanation":"Each English phrase has one Japanese partner with the same meaning. Recheck the complete phrase when two items share a similar word.","explanationJa":"各英文には、同じ意味の日本語が一つずつあります。似た単語がある時も、表現全体の意味で確認しましょう。","prompt":"Match each English phrase with its natural Japanese meaning.","promptJa":"英文と自然な日本語を組み合わせてください。","pairs":[{"en":"I’m annoyed by the noise.","jp":"その音にイライラしています。","cat":"feelings"},{"en":"The noise is annoying.","jp":"その音はイライラさせます。","cat":"feelings"},{"en":"I prefer tea because it’s lighter.","jp":"軽い味なので紅茶の方が好きです。","cat":"preferences"},{"en":"Who do you think will win?","jp":"誰が勝つと思いますか？","cat":"predictions"},{"en":"This exercise is easier than the last one.","jp":"この練習は前のものより簡単です。","cat":"comparisons"},{"en":"They scored in the first half.","jp":"前半に得点しました。","cat":"sports"}]}'::jsonb, false, 6),
    ('june-30', 'june-30-extra-sorting', 35, 'Use It', 'sorting', '{"id":"june-30-extra-sorting","format":"sorting","type":"sorting","section":"Use It","topic":"feelings","isOriginal":false,"hint":"Focus on the feelings meaning. Look for the sentence that expresses “その音はイライラさせます。”.","hintJa":"-ing は原因の性質。","explanation":"The categories describe language purpose: feelings, preferences. Sort by what each complete phrase does in conversation.","explanationJa":"分類は「feelings・preferences」です。単語一つではなく、会話でその表現が果たす役割で分けましょう。","prompt":"Sort each phrase by its language purpose.","promptJa":"各表現を目的別に分類してください。","categories":["feelings","preferences"],"items":[["I’m annoyed by the noise.","feelings"],["The noise is annoying.","feelings"],["I prefer tea because it’s lighter.","preferences"],["I was frustrated because nothing worked.","feelings"]]}'::jsonb, false, 4),
    ('june-30', 'june-30-extra-dialogue', 36, 'Use It', 'dialogue', '{"id":"june-30-extra-dialogue","format":"dialogue","type":"dialogue","section":"Use It","topic":"feelings","isOriginal":false,"hint":"Focus on the feelings meaning. Look for the sentence that expresses “その音はイライラさせます。”.","hintJa":"-ing は原因の性質。","explanation":"“The noise is annoying.” responds directly and naturally to the previous line.","explanationJa":"「The noise is annoying.」は、直前の発言に直接答える自然な一文です。","prompt":"Choose the most natural next line in the conversation.","promptJa":"会話の次に続く最も自然な一文を選んでください。","context":"A: How do you feel about that loud sound?\nB: ...","contextJa":"A：「あの大きな音、どう感じる？」\nB：…","choices":[{"id":"a","en":"The noise is annoying.","jp":"その音はイライラさせます。"},{"id":"b","en":"I prefer tea because it’s lighter.","jp":"軽い味なので紅茶の方が好きです。"},{"id":"c","en":"This exercise is easier than the last one.","jp":"この練習は前のものより簡単です。"},{"id":"d","en":"I was frustrated because nothing worked.","jp":"何もうまくいかず、もどかしかったです。"}],"correct":"a"}'::jsonb, false, 1),
