    ('july-07', 'july-07-draft-order-1', 8, 'Build It', 'order', '{"id":"july-07-draft-order-1","format":"order","type":"order","section":"Build It","topic":"for me","isOriginal":false,"hint":"Focus on the for me meaning. Look for the sentence that expresses “私のためにしてもらえますか？”.","hintJa":"「私のためにしてもらえますか？」を表す英文と、for meの形に注目しましょう。","explanation":"Correct order: “Could you do it for me?”. Build the sentence around the for me pattern.","explanationJa":"正しい語順は「Could you do it for me?」です。for meの形を中心に文を組み立てます。","prompt":"Put the words in order: 私のためにしてもらえますか？","promptJa":"語順を並べましょう：私のためにしてもらえますか？","words":["it","for","me","Could","you","do"],"correctWords":["Could","you","do","it","for","me"]}'::jsonb, false, 1),
    ('july-07', 'july-07-draft-order-2', 9, 'Build It', 'order', '{"id":"july-07-draft-order-2","format":"order","type":"order","section":"Build It","topic":"instead of","isOriginal":false,"hint":"Focus on the instead of meaning. Look for the sentence that expresses “彼が私の代わりに出席しました。”.","hintJa":"「彼が私の代わりに出席しました。」を表す英文と、instead ofの形に注目しましょう。","explanation":"Correct order: “He attended instead of me.”. Build the sentence around the instead of pattern.","explanationJa":"正しい語順は「He attended instead of me.」です。instead ofの形を中心に文を組み立てます。","prompt":"Put the words in order: 彼が私の代わりに出席しました。","promptJa":"語順を並べましょう：彼が私の代わりに出席しました。","words":["attended","me","instead","He","of"],"correctWords":["He","attended","instead","of","me"]}'::jsonb, false, 1),
    ('july-07', 'july-07-draft-matching', 10, 'Build It', 'matching', '{"id":"july-07-draft-matching","format":"matching","type":"matching","section":"Build It","topic":"bring","isOriginal":false,"hint":"Focus on the bring meaning. Look for the sentence that expresses “ノートを持ってきました。”.","hintJa":"「ノートを持ってきました。」を表す英文と、bringの形に注目しましょう。","explanation":"Each English phrase has exactly one Japanese meaning. Match the whole message rather than isolated words.","explanationJa":"各英文に対応する日本語は一つです。単語だけではなく、表現全体の意味で組み合わせましょう。","prompt":"Match the English and Japanese.","promptJa":"英語と日本語を組み合わせてください。","pairs":[{"en":"I brought my notebook.","jp":"ノートを持ってきました。","cat":"bring"},{"en":"I bought a new notebook.","jp":"新しいノートを買いました。","cat":"buy"},{"en":"You told me to do so.","jp":"あなたは私にそうするよう言いました。","cat":"tell"},{"en":"My phone died.","jp":"携帯の充電が切れました。","cat":"daily life"},{"en":"Where will she come from?","jp":"彼女はどこから来ますか？","cat":"questions"},{"en":"I got a flat tire.","jp":"タイヤがパンクしました。","cat":"travel"}]}'::jsonb, false, 6),
    ('july-07', 'july-07-draft-sorting', 11, 'Build It', 'sorting', '{"id":"july-07-draft-sorting","format":"sorting","type":"sorting","section":"Build It","topic":"buy","isOriginal":false,"hint":"Focus on the buy meaning. Look for the sentence that expresses “新しいノートを買いました。”.","hintJa":"「新しいノートを買いました。」を表す英文と、buyの形に注目しましょう。","explanation":"Sort by the purpose of the complete phrase. The available topics are bring, buy, tell.","explanationJa":"英文全体の目的で分類します。今回の分類は「bring・buy・tell」です。","prompt":"Sort the phrases by topic.","promptJa":"表現をトピック別に分類してください。","categories":["bring","buy","tell"],"items":[["I brought my notebook.","bring"],["I bought a new notebook.","buy"],["You told me to do so.","tell"],["Please bring it tomorrow.","bring"]]}'::jsonb, false, 4),
