    ('july-18', 'july-18-draft-speaking-2', 19, 'Speak', 'speaking', '{"id":"july-18-draft-speaking-2","format":"speaking","type":"speaking","section":"Speak","topic":"stove","isOriginal":false,"hint":"Focus on the stove meaning. Look for the sentence that expresses “鍋はコンロにかかっていました。”.","hintJa":"「鍋はコンロにかかっていました。」を表す英文と、stoveの形に注目しましょう。","explanation":"Model: “The pot was on the stove.” (鍋はコンロにかかっていました。). Say it as one connected message, then compare with the model.","explanationJa":"お手本は「The pot was on the stove.」（鍋はコンロにかかっていました。）です。一つの意味のまとまりとして話し、お手本と比べましょう。","prompt":"Listen, then speak.","promptJa":"聞いてから話してみましょう。","speakText":"The pot was on the stove.","speakJa":"鍋はコンロにかかっていました。"}'::jsonb, false, 1),
    ('july-18', 'july-18-draft-speaking-3', 20, 'Speak', 'speaking', '{"id":"july-18-draft-speaking-3","format":"speaking","type":"speaking","section":"Speak","topic":"idiom","isOriginal":false,"hint":"Focus on the idiom meaning. Look for the sentence that expresses “彼は今日は絶好調です。”.","hintJa":"「彼は今日は絶好調です。」を表す英文と、idiomの形に注目しましょう。","explanation":"Model: “He’s on fire today.” (彼は今日は絶好調です。). Say it as one connected message, then compare with the model.","explanationJa":"お手本は「He’s on fire today.」（彼は今日は絶好調です。）です。一つの意味のまとまりとして話し、お手本と比べましょう。","prompt":"Listen, then speak.","promptJa":"聞いてから話してみましょう。","speakText":"He’s on fire today.","speakJa":"彼は今日は絶好調です。"}'::jsonb, false, 1),
    ('july-18', 'july-18-draft-speaking-4', 21, 'Speak', 'speaking', '{"id":"july-18-draft-speaking-4","format":"speaking","type":"speaking","section":"Speak","topic":"have","isOriginal":false,"hint":"Focus on the have meaning. Look for the sentence that expresses “運転免許を持っています。”.","hintJa":"「運転免許を持っています。」を表す英文と、haveの形に注目しましょう。","explanation":"Model: “I have a driver’s license.” (運転免許を持っています。). The second attempt checks whether you can recall the whole phrase independently.","explanationJa":"お手本は「I have a driver’s license.」（運転免許を持っています。）です。2回目は英文を見ずに、表現全体を思い出せるか確認します。","prompt":"Say the sentence naturally, then try it once without looking.","promptJa":"自然に言ってから、英文を見ずにもう一度話してみましょう。","speakText":"I have a driver’s license.","speakJa":"運転免許を持っています。"}'::jsonb, false, 1),
    ('july-18', 'july-18-draft-speaking-5', 22, 'Speak', 'speaking', '{"id":"july-18-draft-speaking-5","format":"speaking","type":"speaking","section":"Speak","topic":"supposed to","isOriginal":false,"hint":"Focus on the supposed to meaning. Look for the sentence that expresses “10時に会うことになっています。”.","hintJa":"「10時に会うことになっています。」を表す英文と、supposed toの形に注目しましょう。","explanation":"Model: “We’re supposed to meet at ten.” (10時に会うことになっています。). The second attempt checks whether you can recall the whole phrase independently.","explanationJa":"お手本は「We’re supposed to meet at ten.」（10時に会うことになっています。）です。2回目は英文を見ずに、表現全体を思い出せるか確認します。","prompt":"Say the sentence naturally, then try it once without looking.","promptJa":"自然に言ってから、英文を見ずにもう一度話してみましょう。","speakText":"We’re supposed to meet at ten.","speakJa":"10時に会うことになっています。"}'::jsonb, false, 1),
    ('july-18', 'july-18-draft-dialogue', 23, 'Use It', 'dialogue', '{"id":"july-18-draft-dialogue","format":"dialogue","type":"dialogue","section":"Use It","topic":"have","isOriginal":false,"hint":"Focus on the have meaning. Look for the sentence that expresses “運転免許を持っています。”.","hintJa":"「運転免許を持っています。」を表す英文と、haveの形に注目しましょう。","explanation":"“Yes, I can. I have a driver’s license.” answers the previous speaker directly and keeps the conversation coherent.","explanationJa":"「Yes, I can. I have a driver’s license.」は直前の発言に直接答え、会話の流れが自然につながります。","prompt":"Choose the most natural next line.","promptJa":"会話の次の一文を選んでください。","context":"A: Can you drive?\nB: ...","contextJa":"A：「運転できますか？」\nB：…","choices":[{"id":"a","en":"Yes, I can. I have a driver’s license.","jp":"はい、できます。運転免許を持っています。"},{"id":"b","en":"Yes, I do drive yesterday.","jp":"はい、昨日運転します。"},{"id":"c","en":"No, I haven’t a license.","jp":"いいえ、免許を持っていません。"},{"id":"d","en":"I’m supposed at ten.","jp":"10時に予定されています。"}],"correct":"a"}'::jsonb, false, 1),
    ('july-18', 'july-18-draft-mistake', 24, 'Use It', 'mistake', '{"id":"july-18-draft-mistake","format":"mistake","type":"mistake","section":"Use It","topic":"supposed to","isOriginal":false,"hint":"Focus on the supposed to meaning. Look for the sentence that expresses “10時に会うことになっています。”.","hintJa":"「10時に会うことになっています。」を表す英文と、supposed toの形に注目しましょう。","explanation":"Correct sentence: “We’re supposed to meet at ten.”. Compare it with the incorrect version and restore the missing or incorrect grammar word.","explanationJa":"正しい英文は「We’re supposed to meet at ten.」です。誤文と比べ、抜けた語や誤った文法部分を直しましょう。","prompt":"Correct the sentence.","promptJa":"英文を自然な形に直してください。","wrongSentence":"We supposed to meet at ten.","accepted":["We’re supposed to meet at ten."]}'::jsonb, false, 1),
    ('july-18', 'july-18-draft-situation', 25, 'Use It', 'situation', '{"id":"july-18-draft-situation","format":"situation","type":"situation","section":"Use It","topic":"feelings","isOriginal":false,"hint":"Focus on the feelings meaning. Look for the sentence that expresses “彼女は気合いが入って準備万端です。”.","hintJa":"「彼女は気合いが入って準備万端です。」を表す英文と、feelingsの形に注目しましょう。","explanation":"“She’s fired up and ready.” directly expresses “彼女は気合いが入って準備万端です。”. The other choices answer different situations.","explanationJa":"「She’s fired up and ready.」が「彼女は気合いが入って準備万端です。」を直接表します。他の選択肢は別の場面に使う表現です。","prompt":"Which sentence would you use when you want to say: 彼女は気合いが入って準備万端です。","promptJa":"「彼女は気合いが入って準備万端です。」と言いたい時、どの英文を使いますか？","choices":[{"id":"a","en":"She’s fired up and ready.","jp":"彼女は気合いが入って準備万端です。"},{"id":"b","en":"I was supposed to join the class.","jp":"そのクラスに参加する予定でした。"},{"id":"c","en":"She hasn’t eaten yet.","jp":"彼女はまだ食べていません。"},{"id":"d","en":"The house is on fire.","jp":"家が燃えています。"}],"correct":"a"}'::jsonb, false, 1),
    ('july-18', 'july-18-draft-visual-1', 26, 'See It', 'situation', '{"id":"july-18-draft-visual-1","format":"situation","type":"situation","section":"See It","topic":"has","isOriginal":false,"hint":"Use the visible action and objects as evidence: A woman happily holds her pet cat at home. Choose the sentence that describes that complete scene.","hintJa":"イラストの人物の動作や物を確認し、「彼女は猫を飼っています。」に合う場面か考えましょう。場面全体を説明する英文を選んでください。","explanation":"The illustration shows this scene: A woman happily holds her pet cat at home. That directly matches “She has a cat.” (彼女は猫を飼っています。); the other choices describe different actions or situations.","explanationJa":"イラストの人物の動作や物が「彼女は猫を飼っています。」という場面を表しています。そのため「She has a cat.」が一致し、他の選択肢は別の動作・場面を表します。","prompt":"Which sentence best matches the illustration?","promptJa":"イラストの場面に最も合う英文を選んでください。","choices":[{"id":"a","en":"She has a cat.","jp":"彼女は猫を飼っています。"},{"id":"b","en":"She doesn’t have a cat.","jp":"彼女は猫を飼っていません。"},{"id":"c","en":"The pot was on the stove.","jp":"鍋はコンロにかかっていました。"},{"id":"d","en":"I have a driver’s license.","jp":"運転免許を持っています。"}],"correct":"a","image":"/assets/questions/visual/july-18-01-has-cat.webp","imageAlt":"A woman happily holds her pet cat at home.","visualAssetId":"july-18-01"}'::jsonb, false, 1),
    ('july-18', 'july-18-draft-visual-2', 27, 'See It', 'situation', '{"id":"july-18-draft-visual-2","format":"situation","type":"situation","section":"See It","topic":"stove","isOriginal":false,"hint":"Use the visible action and objects as evidence: A cooking pot sits safely on the stove. Choose the sentence that describes that complete scene.","hintJa":"イラストの人物の動作や物を確認し、「鍋はコンロにかかっていました。」に合う場面か考えましょう。場面全体を説明する英文を選んでください。","explanation":"The illustration shows this scene: A cooking pot sits safely on the stove. That directly matches “The pot was on the stove.” (鍋はコンロにかかっていました。); the other choices describe different actions or situations.","explanationJa":"イラストの人物の動作や物が「鍋はコンロにかかっていました。」という場面を表しています。そのため「The pot was on the stove.」が一致し、他の選択肢は別の動作・場面を表します。","prompt":"Which sentence best matches the illustration?","promptJa":"イラストの場面に最も合う英文を選んでください。","choices":[{"id":"a","en":"The pot was on the stove.","jp":"鍋はコンロにかかっていました。"},{"id":"b","en":"The pot caught fire.","jp":"鍋に火がつきました。"},{"id":"c","en":"I have a driver’s license.","jp":"運転免許を持っています。"},{"id":"d","en":"She has a cat.","jp":"彼女は猫を飼っています。"}],"correct":"a","image":"/assets/questions/visual/july-18-02-pot-on-stove.webp","imageAlt":"A cooking pot sits safely on the stove.","visualAssetId":"july-18-02"}'::jsonb, false, 1),
    ('july-18', 'july-18-draft-visual-3', 28, 'See It', 'situation', '{"id":"july-18-draft-visual-3","format":"situation","type":"situation","section":"See It","topic":"fire","isOriginal":false,"hint":"Use the visible action and objects as evidence: A cooking pot has caught fire on the stove. Choose the sentence that describes that complete scene.","hintJa":"イラストの人物の動作や物を確認し、「鍋に火がつきました。」に合う場面か考えましょう。場面全体を説明する英文を選んでください。","explanation":"The illustration shows this scene: A cooking pot has caught fire on the stove. That directly matches “The pot caught fire.” (鍋に火がつきました。); the other choices describe different actions or situations.","explanationJa":"イラストの人物の動作や物が「鍋に火がつきました。」という場面を表しています。そのため「The pot caught fire.」が一致し、他の選択肢は別の動作・場面を表します。","prompt":"Which sentence best matches the illustration?","promptJa":"イラストの場面に最も合う英文を選んでください。","choices":[{"id":"a","en":"The pot caught fire.","jp":"鍋に火がつきました。"},{"id":"b","en":"The house is on fire.","jp":"家が燃えています。"},{"id":"c","en":"We’re supposed to meet at ten.","jp":"10時に会うことになっています。"},{"id":"d","en":"She doesn’t have a cat.","jp":"彼女は猫を飼っていません。"}],"correct":"a","image":"/assets/questions/visual/july-18-03-pot-caught-fire.webp","imageAlt":"A cooking pot has caught fire on the stove.","visualAssetId":"july-18-03"}'::jsonb, false, 1),
    ('july-18', 'july-18-draft-visual-4', 29, 'See It', 'situation', '{"id":"july-18-draft-visual-4","format":"situation","type":"situation","section":"See It","topic":"fire","isOriginal":false,"hint":"Use the visible action and objects as evidence: Firefighters respond to a house on fire. Choose the sentence that describes that complete scene.","hintJa":"イラストの人物の動作や物を確認し、「家が燃えています。」に合う場面か考えましょう。場面全体を説明する英文を選んでください。","explanation":"The illustration shows this scene: Firefighters respond to a house on fire. That directly matches “The house is on fire.” (家が燃えています。); the other choices describe different actions or situations.","explanationJa":"イラストの人物の動作や物が「家が燃えています。」という場面を表しています。そのため「The house is on fire.」が一致し、他の選択肢は別の動作・場面を表します。","prompt":"Which sentence best matches the illustration?","promptJa":"イラストの場面に最も合う英文を選んでください。","choices":[{"id":"a","en":"The house is on fire.","jp":"家が燃えています。"},{"id":"b","en":"He’s on fire today.","jp":"彼は今日は絶好調です。"},{"id":"c","en":"She’s fired up and ready.","jp":"彼女は気合いが入って準備万端です。"},{"id":"d","en":"She hasn’t eaten yet.","jp":"彼女はまだ食べていません。"}],"correct":"a","image":"/assets/questions/visual/july-18-04-house-on-fire.webp","imageAlt":"Firefighters respond to a house on fire.","visualAssetId":"july-18-04"}'::jsonb, false, 1),
    ('july-18', 'july-18-draft-visual-5', 30, 'See It', 'situation', '{"id":"july-18-draft-visual-5","format":"situation","type":"situation","section":"See It","topic":"idiom","isOriginal":false,"hint":"Use the visible action and objects as evidence: An athlete performs brilliantly and celebrates a winning streak. Choose the sentence that describes that complete scene.","hintJa":"イラストの人物の動作や物を確認し、「彼は今日は絶好調です。」に合う場面か考えましょう。場面全体を説明する英文を選んでください。","explanation":"The illustration shows this scene: An athlete performs brilliantly and celebrates a winning streak. That directly matches “He’s on fire today.” (彼は今日は絶好調です。); the other choices describe different actions or situations.","explanationJa":"イラストの人物の動作や物が「彼は今日は絶好調です。」という場面を表しています。そのため「He’s on fire today.」が一致し、他の選択肢は別の動作・場面を表します。","prompt":"Which sentence best matches the illustration?","promptJa":"イラストの場面に最も合う英文を選んでください。","choices":[{"id":"a","en":"He’s on fire today.","jp":"彼は今日は絶好調です。"},{"id":"b","en":"I have a driver’s license.","jp":"運転免許を持っています。"},{"id":"c","en":"I was supposed to join the class.","jp":"そのクラスに参加する予定でした。"},{"id":"d","en":"I do like this song.","jp":"この歌は本当に好きです。"}],"correct":"a","image":"/assets/questions/visual/july-18-05-on-fire-idiom.webp","imageAlt":"An athlete performs brilliantly and celebrates a winning streak.","visualAssetId":"july-18-05"}'::jsonb, false, 1),
    ('july-19', 'july-19-draft-choice-1', 0, 'Understand', 'mcq', '{"id":"july-19-draft-choice-1","format":"mcq","type":"mcq","section":"Understand","topic":"both","isOriginal":false,"hint":"Focus on the both meaning. Look for the sentence that expresses “紅茶もコーヒーも両方好きです。”.","hintJa":"「紅茶もコーヒーも両方好きです。」を表す英文と、bothの形に注目しましょう。","explanation":"“I like both tea and coffee.” is the sentence that means “紅茶もコーヒーも両方好きです。”. Check the complete meaning before choosing.","explanationJa":"「I like both tea and coffee.」が「紅茶もコーヒーも両方好きです。」を表す英文です。単語一つではなく文全体の意味で選びましょう。","prompt":"Choose the English sentence that means: 紅茶もコーヒーも両方好きです。","promptJa":"「紅茶もコーヒーも両方好きです。」に合う英文を選んでください。","choices":[{"id":"a","en":"I like both tea and coffee.","jp":"紅茶もコーヒーも両方好きです。"},{"id":"b","en":"Either day works for me.","jp":"どちらの日でも大丈夫です。"},{"id":"c","en":"I’d rather stay home than go out.","jp":"外出するより家にいたいです。"},{"id":"d","en":"I ran into an old friend.","jp":"昔の友人に偶然会いました。"}],"correct":"a"}'::jsonb, false, 1),
    ('july-19', 'july-19-draft-choice-2', 1, 'Understand', 'mcq', '{"id":"july-19-draft-choice-2","format":"mcq","type":"mcq","section":"Understand","topic":"either","isOriginal":false,"hint":"Focus on the either meaning. Look for the sentence that expresses “どちらの日でも大丈夫です。”.","hintJa":"「どちらの日でも大丈夫です。」を表す英文と、eitherの形に注目しましょう。","explanation":"“Either day works for me.” is the sentence that means “どちらの日でも大丈夫です。”. Check the complete meaning before choosing.","explanationJa":"「Either day works for me.」が「どちらの日でも大丈夫です。」を表す英文です。単語一つではなく文全体の意味で選びましょう。","prompt":"Choose the English sentence that means: どちらの日でも大丈夫です。","promptJa":"「どちらの日でも大丈夫です。」に合う英文を選んでください。","choices":[{"id":"a","en":"Either day works for me.","jp":"どちらの日でも大丈夫です。"},{"id":"b","en":"I like neither option.","jp":"どちらの選択肢も好きではありません。"},{"id":"c","en":"I’d rather not talk about it.","jp":"できればその話はしたくありません。"},{"id":"d","en":"I’m on my way to work.","jp":"仕事へ向かっている途中です。"}],"correct":"a"}'::jsonb, false, 1),
    ('july-19', 'july-19-draft-choice-3', 2, 'Understand', 'mcq', '{"id":"july-19-draft-choice-3","format":"mcq","type":"mcq","section":"Understand","topic":"neither","isOriginal":false,"hint":"Focus on the neither meaning. Look for the sentence that expresses “どちらの選択肢も好きではありません。”.","hintJa":"「どちらの選択肢も好きではありません。」を表す英文と、neitherの形に注目しましょう。","explanation":"“I like neither option.” is the sentence that means “どちらの選択肢も好きではありません。”. Check the complete meaning before choosing.","explanationJa":"「I like neither option.」が「どちらの選択肢も好きではありません。」を表す英文です。単語一つではなく文全体の意味で選びましょう。","prompt":"Choose the English sentence that means: どちらの選択肢も好きではありません。","promptJa":"「どちらの選択肢も好きではありません。」に合う英文を選んでください。","choices":[{"id":"a","en":"I like neither option.","jp":"どちらの選択肢も好きではありません。"},{"id":"b","en":"I don’t like either.","jp":"どちらも好きではありません。"},{"id":"c","en":"That was hilarious.","jp":"それは爆笑するほど面白かったです。"},{"id":"d","en":"I won’t have coffee.","jp":"コーヒーは飲みません。"}],"correct":"a"}'::jsonb, false, 1),
    ('july-19', 'july-19-draft-choice-4', 3, 'Understand', 'mcq', '{"id":"july-19-draft-choice-4","format":"mcq","type":"mcq","section":"Understand","topic":"either","isOriginal":false,"hint":"Focus on the either meaning. Look for the sentence that expresses “どちらも好きではありません。”.","hintJa":"「どちらも好きではありません。」を表す英文と、eitherの形に注目しましょう。","explanation":"“I don’t like either.” is the sentence that means “どちらも好きではありません。”. Check the complete meaning before choosing.","explanationJa":"「I don’t like either.」が「どちらも好きではありません。」を表す英文です。単語一つではなく文全体の意味で選びましょう。","prompt":"Choose the English sentence that means: どちらも好きではありません。","promptJa":"「どちらも好きではありません。」に合う英文を選んでください。","choices":[{"id":"a","en":"I don’t like either.","jp":"どちらも好きではありません。"},{"id":"b","en":"I’d rather stay home than go out.","jp":"外出するより家にいたいです。"},{"id":"c","en":"That joke cracked me up.","jp":"その冗談で爆笑しました。"},{"id":"d","en":"I want to have coffee.","jp":"コーヒーを飲みたいです。"}],"correct":"a"}'::jsonb, false, 1),
    ('july-19', 'july-19-draft-true-false-1', 4, 'Understand', 'truefalse', '{"id":"july-19-draft-true-false-1","format":"truefalse","type":"truefalse","section":"Understand","topic":"would rather","isOriginal":false,"hint":"Focus on the would rather meaning. Look for the sentence that expresses “外出するより家にいたいです。”.","hintJa":"「外出するより家にいたいです。」を表す英文と、would ratherの形に注目しましょう。","explanation":"True. “I’d rather stay home than go out.” means “外出するより家にいたいです。”.","explanationJa":"正解はTrueです。「I’d rather stay home than go out.」は「外出するより家にいたいです。」という意味です。","prompt":"“I’d rather stay home than go out.” means “外出するより家にいたいです。”.","promptJa":"「I’d rather stay home than go out.」は「外出するより家にいたいです。」という意味です。","correct":true}'::jsonb, false, 1),
    ('july-19', 'july-19-draft-true-false-2', 5, 'Understand', 'truefalse', '{"id":"july-19-draft-true-false-2","format":"truefalse","type":"truefalse","section":"Understand","topic":"rather not","isOriginal":false,"hint":"Focus on the rather not meaning. Look for the sentence that expresses “できればその話はしたくありません。”.","hintJa":"「できればその話はしたくありません。」を表す英文と、rather notの形に注目しましょう。","explanation":"False. “I’d rather not talk about it.” means “できればその話はしたくありません。”, not “それは爆笑するほど面白かったです。”.","explanationJa":"正解はFalseです。「I’d rather not talk about it.」は「できればその話はしたくありません。」であり、「それは爆笑するほど面白かったです。」ではありません。","prompt":"“I’d rather not talk about it.” means “それは爆笑するほど面白かったです。”.","promptJa":"「I’d rather not talk about it.」は「それは爆笑するほど面白かったです。」という意味です。","correct":false}'::jsonb, false, 1),
    ('july-19', 'july-19-draft-typed-1', 6, 'Build It', 'translation', '{"id":"july-19-draft-typed-1","format":"translation","type":"translation","section":"Build It","topic":"hilarious","isOriginal":false,"hint":"Focus on the hilarious meaning. Look for the sentence that expresses “それは爆笑するほど面白かったです。”.","hintJa":"「それは爆笑するほど面白かったです。」を表す英文と、hilariousの形に注目しましょう。","explanation":"A natural translation is “That was hilarious.”. It expresses “それは爆笑するほど面白かったです。” with the lesson’s hilarious pattern.","explanationJa":"自然な英訳は「That was hilarious.」です。「それは爆笑するほど面白かったです。」を今回のhilarious表現で伝えています。","prompt":"Translate into English: それは爆笑するほど面白かったです。","promptJa":"英語にしてください：それは爆笑するほど面白かったです。","accepted":["That was hilarious."]}'::jsonb, false, 1),
    ('july-19', 'july-19-draft-typed-2', 7, 'Build It', 'translation', '{"id":"july-19-draft-typed-2","format":"translation","type":"translation","section":"Build It","topic":"crack up","isOriginal":false,"hint":"Focus on the crack up meaning. Look for the sentence that expresses “その冗談で爆笑しました。”.","hintJa":"「その冗談で爆笑しました。」を表す英文と、crack upの形に注目しましょう。","explanation":"A natural translation is “That joke cracked me up.”. It expresses “その冗談で爆笑しました。” with the lesson’s crack up pattern.","explanationJa":"自然な英訳は「That joke cracked me up.」です。「その冗談で爆笑しました。」を今回のcrack up表現で伝えています。","prompt":"Translate into English: その冗談で爆笑しました。","promptJa":"英語にしてください：その冗談で爆笑しました。","accepted":["That joke cracked me up."]}'::jsonb, false, 1),
    ('july-19', 'july-19-draft-order-1', 8, 'Build It', 'order', '{"id":"july-19-draft-order-1","format":"order","type":"order","section":"Build It","topic":"run into","isOriginal":false,"hint":"Focus on the run into meaning. Look for the sentence that expresses “昔の友人に偶然会いました。”.","hintJa":"「昔の友人に偶然会いました。」を表す英文と、run intoの形に注目しましょう。","explanation":"Correct order: “I ran into an old friend.”. Build the sentence around the run into pattern.","explanationJa":"正しい語順は「I ran into an old friend.」です。run intoの形を中心に文を組み立てます。","prompt":"Put the words in order: 昔の友人に偶然会いました。","promptJa":"語順を並べましょう：昔の友人に偶然会いました。","words":["an","old","friend","I","ran","into"],"correctWords":["I","ran","into","an","old","friend"]}'::jsonb, false, 1),
    ('july-19', 'july-19-draft-order-2', 9, 'Build It', 'order', '{"id":"july-19-draft-order-2","format":"order","type":"order","section":"Build It","topic":"on my way","isOriginal":false,"hint":"Focus on the on my way meaning. Look for the sentence that expresses “仕事へ向かっている途中です。”.","hintJa":"「仕事へ向かっている途中です。」を表す英文と、on my wayの形に注目しましょう。","explanation":"Correct order: “I’m on my way to work.”. Build the sentence around the on my way pattern.","explanationJa":"正しい語順は「I’m on my way to work.」です。on my wayの形を中心に文を組み立てます。","prompt":"Put the words in order: 仕事へ向かっている途中です。","promptJa":"語順を並べましょう：仕事へ向かっている途中です。","words":["way","to","work","I’m","on","my"],"correctWords":["I’m","on","my","way","to","work"]}'::jsonb, false, 1),
    ('july-19', 'july-19-draft-matching', 10, 'Build It', 'matching', '{"id":"july-19-draft-matching","format":"matching","type":"matching","section":"Build It","topic":"both","isOriginal":false,"hint":"Focus on the both meaning. Look for the sentence that expresses “紅茶もコーヒーも両方好きです。”.","hintJa":"「紅茶もコーヒーも両方好きです。」を表す英文と、bothの形に注目しましょう。","explanation":"Each English phrase has exactly one Japanese meaning. Match the whole message rather than isolated words.","explanationJa":"各英文に対応する日本語は一つです。単語だけではなく、表現全体の意味で組み合わせましょう。","prompt":"Match the English and Japanese.","promptJa":"英語と日本語を組み合わせてください。","pairs":[{"en":"I like both tea and coffee.","jp":"紅茶もコーヒーも両方好きです。","cat":"both"},{"en":"Either day works for me.","jp":"どちらの日でも大丈夫です。","cat":"either"},{"en":"I like neither option.","jp":"どちらの選択肢も好きではありません。","cat":"neither"},{"en":"I don’t like either.","jp":"どちらも好きではありません。","cat":"either"},{"en":"I’d rather stay home than go out.","jp":"外出するより家にいたいです。","cat":"would rather"},{"en":"I’d rather not talk about it.","jp":"できればその話はしたくありません。","cat":"rather not"}]}'::jsonb, false, 6),
    ('july-19', 'july-19-draft-sorting', 11, 'Build It', 'sorting', '{"id":"july-19-draft-sorting","format":"sorting","type":"sorting","section":"Build It","topic":"either","isOriginal":false,"hint":"Focus on the either meaning. Look for the sentence that expresses “どちらの日でも大丈夫です。”.","hintJa":"「どちらの日でも大丈夫です。」を表す英文と、eitherの形に注目しましょう。","explanation":"Sort by the purpose of the complete phrase. The available topics are both, either, neither.","explanationJa":"英文全体の目的で分類します。今回の分類は「both・either・neither」です。","prompt":"Sort the phrases by topic.","promptJa":"表現をトピック別に分類してください。","categories":["both","either","neither"],"items":[["I like both tea and coffee.","both"],["Either day works for me.","either"],["I like neither option.","neither"],["I don’t like either.","either"]]}'::jsonb, false, 4),
    ('july-19', 'july-19-draft-listen-choice-1', 12, 'Listen', 'listenChoice', '{"id":"july-19-draft-listen-choice-1","format":"listenChoice","type":"listenChoice","section":"Listen","topic":"both","isOriginal":false,"hint":"Focus on the both meaning. Look for the sentence that expresses “紅茶もコーヒーも両方好きです。”.","hintJa":"「紅茶もコーヒーも両方好きです。」を表す英文と、bothの形に注目しましょう。","explanation":"The sentence in the audio is “I like both tea and coffee.”. Listen through to the end before choosing.","explanationJa":"音声の英文は「I like both tea and coffee.」です。最後まで聞いてから選びましょう。","prompt":"Listen and choose the sentence.","promptJa":"音声を聞いて英文を選んでください。","audioText":"I like both tea and coffee.","choices":[{"id":"a","en":"I like both tea and coffee.","jp":"紅茶もコーヒーも両方好きです。"},{"id":"b","en":"Either day works for me.","jp":"どちらの日でも大丈夫です。"},{"id":"c","en":"I’d rather stay home than go out.","jp":"外出するより家にいたいです。"},{"id":"d","en":"I ran into an old friend.","jp":"昔の友人に偶然会いました。"}],"correct":"a"}'::jsonb, false, 1),
