    ('july-26', 'july-26-draft-speaking-3', 20, 'Speak', 'speaking', '{"id":"july-26-draft-speaking-3","format":"speaking","type":"speaking","section":"Speak","topic":"past perfect","isOriginal":false,"hint":"Focus on the past perfect meaning. Look for the sentence that expresses “彼が電話する前に夕食を終えていました。”.","hintJa":"「彼が電話する前に夕食を終えていました。」を表す英文と、past perfectの形に注目しましょう。","explanation":"Model: “I had finished dinner before he called.” (彼が電話する前に夕食を終えていました。). Say it as one connected message, then compare with the model.","explanationJa":"お手本は「I had finished dinner before he called.」（彼が電話する前に夕食を終えていました。）です。一つの意味のまとまりとして話し、お手本と比べましょう。","prompt":"Listen, then speak.","promptJa":"聞いてから話してみましょう。","speakText":"I had finished dinner before he called.","speakJa":"彼が電話する前に夕食を終えていました。"}'::jsonb, false, 1),
    ('july-26', 'july-26-draft-speaking-4', 21, 'Speak', 'speaking', '{"id":"july-26-draft-speaking-4","format":"speaking","type":"speaking","section":"Speak","topic":"past perfect","isOriginal":false,"hint":"Focus on the past perfect meaning. Look for the sentence that expresses “あなたが到着した時にはもう食べていました。”.","hintJa":"「あなたが到着した時にはもう食べていました。」を表す英文と、past perfectの形に注目しましょう。","explanation":"Model: “I had already eaten when you arrived.” (あなたが到着した時にはもう食べていました。). The second attempt checks whether you can recall the whole phrase independently.","explanationJa":"お手本は「I had already eaten when you arrived.」（あなたが到着した時にはもう食べていました。）です。2回目は英文を見ずに、表現全体を思い出せるか確認します。","prompt":"Say the sentence naturally, then try it once without looking.","promptJa":"自然に言ってから、英文を見ずにもう一度話してみましょう。","speakText":"I had already eaten when you arrived.","speakJa":"あなたが到着した時にはもう食べていました。"}'::jsonb, false, 1),
    ('july-26', 'july-26-draft-speaking-5', 22, 'Speak', 'speaking', '{"id":"july-26-draft-speaking-5","format":"speaking","type":"speaking","section":"Speak","topic":"bath","isOriginal":false,"hint":"Focus on the bath meaning. Look for the sentence that expresses “まだお風呂に入っていません。”.","hintJa":"「まだお風呂に入っていません。」を表す英文と、bathの形に注目しましょう。","explanation":"Model: “I haven’t taken a bath yet.” (まだお風呂に入っていません。). The second attempt checks whether you can recall the whole phrase independently.","explanationJa":"お手本は「I haven’t taken a bath yet.」（まだお風呂に入っていません。）です。2回目は英文を見ずに、表現全体を思い出せるか確認します。","prompt":"Say the sentence naturally, then try it once without looking.","promptJa":"自然に言ってから、英文を見ずにもう一度話してみましょう。","speakText":"I haven’t taken a bath yet.","speakJa":"まだお風呂に入っていません。"}'::jsonb, false, 1),
    ('july-26', 'july-26-draft-dialogue', 23, 'Use It', 'dialogue', '{"id":"july-26-draft-dialogue","format":"dialogue","type":"dialogue","section":"Use It","topic":"past perfect","isOriginal":false,"hint":"Focus on the past perfect meaning. Look for the sentence that expresses “あなたが到着した時にはもう食べていました。”.","hintJa":"「あなたが到着した時にはもう食べていました。」を表す英文と、past perfectの形に注目しましょう。","explanation":"“I had already eaten when you arrived.” answers the previous speaker directly and keeps the conversation coherent.","explanationJa":"「I had already eaten when you arrived.」は直前の発言に直接答え、会話の流れが自然につながります。","prompt":"Choose the most natural next line.","promptJa":"会話の次の一文を選んでください。","context":"A: Why didn’t you eat with us?\nB: ...","contextJa":"A：「どうして一緒に食べなかったの？」\nB：…","choices":[{"id":"a","en":"I had already eaten when you arrived.","jp":"あなたが到着した時にはもう食べていました。"},{"id":"b","en":"I haven’t taken a bath yet.","jp":"まだお風呂に入っていません。"},{"id":"c","en":"I wish I were in Malaysia now.","jp":"今マレーシアにいたらいいのに。"},{"id":"d","en":"I haven’t eaten dinner yet.","jp":"まだ夕食を食べていません。"}],"correct":"a"}'::jsonb, false, 1),
    ('july-26', 'july-26-draft-mistake', 24, 'Use It', 'mistake', '{"id":"july-26-draft-mistake","format":"mistake","type":"mistake","section":"Use It","topic":"bath","isOriginal":false,"hint":"Focus on the bath meaning. Look for the sentence that expresses “まだお風呂に入っていません。”.","hintJa":"「まだお風呂に入っていません。」を表す英文と、bathの形に注目しましょう。","explanation":"Correct sentence: “I haven’t taken a bath yet.”. Compare it with the incorrect version and restore the missing or incorrect grammar word.","explanationJa":"正しい英文は「I haven’t taken a bath yet.」です。誤文と比べ、抜けた語や誤った文法部分を直しましょう。","prompt":"Correct the sentence.","promptJa":"英文を自然な形に直してください。","wrongSentence":"I taken a bath yet.","accepted":["I haven’t taken a bath yet."]}'::jsonb, false, 1),
    ('july-26', 'july-26-draft-situation', 25, 'Use It', 'situation', '{"id":"july-26-draft-situation","format":"situation","type":"situation","section":"Use It","topic":"past","isOriginal":false,"hint":"Focus on the past meaning. Look for the sentence that expresses “昨夜はお風呂に入りませんでした。”.","hintJa":"「昨夜はお風呂に入りませんでした。」を表す英文と、pastの形に注目しましょう。","explanation":"“I didn’t take a bath last night.” directly expresses “昨夜はお風呂に入りませんでした。”. The other choices answer different situations.","explanationJa":"「I didn’t take a bath last night.」が「昨夜はお風呂に入りませんでした。」を直接表します。他の選択肢は別の場面に使う表現です。","prompt":"Which sentence would you use when you want to say: 昨夜はお風呂に入りませんでした。","promptJa":"「昨夜はお風呂に入りませんでした。」と言いたい時、どの英文を使いますか？","choices":[{"id":"a","en":"I didn’t take a bath last night.","jp":"昨夜はお風呂に入りませんでした。"},{"id":"b","en":"I hope I can visit Malaysia next year.","jp":"来年マレーシアへ行けるといいな。"},{"id":"c","en":"I wish I had been born there.","jp":"そこで生まれていたらよかった。"},{"id":"d","en":"I have lived here since 2016.","jp":"2016年からここに住んでいます。"}],"correct":"a"}'::jsonb, false, 1),
    ('july-26', 'july-26-draft-visual-1', 26, 'See It', 'situation', '{"id":"july-26-draft-visual-1","format":"situation","type":"situation","section":"See It","topic":"hope","isOriginal":false,"hint":"Use the visible action and objects as evidence: A hopeful traveler plans to visit Malaysia next year. Choose the sentence that describes that complete scene.","hintJa":"イラストの人物の動作や物を確認し、「来年マレーシアへ行けるといいな。」に合う場面か考えましょう。場面全体を説明する英文を選んでください。","explanation":"The illustration shows this scene: A hopeful traveler plans to visit Malaysia next year. That directly matches “I hope I can visit Malaysia next year.” (来年マレーシアへ行けるといいな。); the other choices describe different actions or situations.","explanationJa":"イラストの人物の動作や物が「来年マレーシアへ行けるといいな。」という場面を表しています。そのため「I hope I can visit Malaysia next year.」が一致し、他の選択肢は別の動作・場面を表します。","prompt":"Which sentence best matches the illustration?","promptJa":"イラストの場面に最も合う英文を選んでください。","choices":[{"id":"a","en":"I hope I can visit Malaysia next year.","jp":"来年マレーシアへ行けるといいな。"},{"id":"b","en":"I have already eaten breakfast.","jp":"もう朝食を食べました。"},{"id":"c","en":"I have lived here since 2016.","jp":"2016年からここに住んでいます。"},{"id":"d","en":"I haven’t taken a bath yet.","jp":"まだお風呂に入っていません。"}],"correct":"a","image":"/assets/questions/visual/july-26-01-hope-malaysia.webp","imageAlt":"A hopeful traveler plans to visit Malaysia next year.","visualAssetId":"july-26-01"}'::jsonb, false, 1),
    ('july-26', 'july-26-draft-visual-2', 27, 'See It', 'situation', '{"id":"july-26-draft-visual-2","format":"situation","type":"situation","section":"See It","topic":"wish","isOriginal":false,"hint":"Use the visible action and objects as evidence: A person in a rainy room wishes they were in sunny Malaysia. Choose the sentence that describes that complete scene.","hintJa":"イラストの人物の動作や物を確認し、「今マレーシアにいたらいいのに。」に合う場面か考えましょう。場面全体を説明する英文を選んでください。","explanation":"The illustration shows this scene: A person in a rainy room wishes they were in sunny Malaysia. That directly matches “I wish I were in Malaysia now.” (今マレーシアにいたらいいのに。); the other choices describe different actions or situations.","explanationJa":"イラストの人物の動作や物が「今マレーシアにいたらいいのに。」という場面を表しています。そのため「I wish I were in Malaysia now.」が一致し、他の選択肢は別の動作・場面を表します。","prompt":"Which sentence best matches the illustration?","promptJa":"イラストの場面に最も合う英文を選んでください。","choices":[{"id":"a","en":"I wish I were in Malaysia now.","jp":"今マレーシアにいたらいいのに。"},{"id":"b","en":"I wish I had studied harder.","jp":"もっと勉強しておけばよかった。"},{"id":"c","en":"I haven’t eaten dinner yet.","jp":"まだ夕食を食べていません。"},{"id":"d","en":"I had already eaten when you arrived.","jp":"あなたが到着した時にはもう食べていました。"}],"correct":"a","image":"/assets/questions/visual/july-26-02-wish-in-malaysia.webp","imageAlt":"A person in a rainy room wishes they were in sunny Malaysia.","visualAssetId":"july-26-02"}'::jsonb, false, 1),
    ('july-26', 'july-26-draft-visual-3', 28, 'See It', 'situation', '{"id":"july-26-draft-visual-3","format":"situation","type":"situation","section":"See It","topic":"regret","isOriginal":false,"hint":"Use the visible action and objects as evidence: A learner regrets not studying harder before a test. Choose the sentence that describes that complete scene.","hintJa":"イラストの人物の動作や物を確認し、「もっと勉強しておけばよかった。」に合う場面か考えましょう。場面全体を説明する英文を選んでください。","explanation":"The illustration shows this scene: A learner regrets not studying harder before a test. That directly matches “I wish I had studied harder.” (もっと勉強しておけばよかった。); the other choices describe different actions or situations.","explanationJa":"イラストの人物の動作や物が「もっと勉強しておけばよかった。」という場面を表しています。そのため「I wish I had studied harder.」が一致し、他の選択肢は別の動作・場面を表します。","prompt":"Which sentence best matches the illustration?","promptJa":"イラストの場面に最も合う英文を選んでください。","choices":[{"id":"a","en":"I wish I had studied harder.","jp":"もっと勉強しておけばよかった。"},{"id":"b","en":"I wish I had been born there.","jp":"そこで生まれていたらよかった。"},{"id":"c","en":"I’ve just arrived home.","jp":"たった今家に着きました。"},{"id":"d","en":"I haven’t taken a bath yet.","jp":"まだお風呂に入っていません。"}],"correct":"a","image":"/assets/questions/visual/july-26-03-studied-harder.webp","imageAlt":"A learner regrets not studying harder before a test.","visualAssetId":"july-26-03"}'::jsonb, false, 1),
    ('july-26', 'july-26-draft-visual-4', 29, 'See It', 'situation', '{"id":"july-26-draft-visual-4","format":"situation","type":"situation","section":"See It","topic":"present perfect","isOriginal":false,"hint":"Use the visible action and objects as evidence: A person has already finished breakfast. Choose the sentence that describes that complete scene.","hintJa":"イラストの人物の動作や物を確認し、「もう朝食を食べました。」に合う場面か考えましょう。場面全体を説明する英文を選んでください。","explanation":"The illustration shows this scene: A person has already finished breakfast. That directly matches “I have already eaten breakfast.” (もう朝食を食べました。); the other choices describe different actions or situations.","explanationJa":"イラストの人物の動作や物が「もう朝食を食べました。」という場面を表しています。そのため「I have already eaten breakfast.」が一致し、他の選択肢は別の動作・場面を表します。","prompt":"Which sentence best matches the illustration?","promptJa":"イラストの場面に最も合う英文を選んでください。","choices":[{"id":"a","en":"I have already eaten breakfast.","jp":"もう朝食を食べました。"},{"id":"b","en":"I haven’t eaten dinner yet.","jp":"まだ夕食を食べていません。"},{"id":"c","en":"I had finished dinner before he called.","jp":"彼が電話する前に夕食を終えていました。"},{"id":"d","en":"I hope I can visit Malaysia next year.","jp":"来年マレーシアへ行けるといいな。"}],"correct":"a","image":"/assets/questions/visual/july-26-04-already-breakfast.webp","imageAlt":"A person has already finished breakfast.","visualAssetId":"july-26-04"}'::jsonb, false, 1),
    ('july-26', 'july-26-draft-visual-5', 30, 'See It', 'situation', '{"id":"july-26-draft-visual-5","format":"situation","type":"situation","section":"See It","topic":"past perfect","isOriginal":false,"hint":"Use the visible action and objects as evidence: Dinner was finished before a phone call arrived. Choose the sentence that describes that complete scene.","hintJa":"イラストの人物の動作や物を確認し、「彼が電話する前に夕食を終えていました。」に合う場面か考えましょう。場面全体を説明する英文を選んでください。","explanation":"The illustration shows this scene: Dinner was finished before a phone call arrived. That directly matches “I had finished dinner before he called.” (彼が電話する前に夕食を終えていました。); the other choices describe different actions or situations.","explanationJa":"イラストの人物の動作や物が「彼が電話する前に夕食を終えていました。」という場面を表しています。そのため「I had finished dinner before he called.」が一致し、他の選択肢は別の動作・場面を表します。","prompt":"Which sentence best matches the illustration?","promptJa":"イラストの場面に最も合う英文を選んでください。","choices":[{"id":"a","en":"I had finished dinner before he called.","jp":"彼が電話する前に夕食を終えていました。"},{"id":"b","en":"I hope I can visit Malaysia next year.","jp":"来年マレーシアへ行けるといいな。"},{"id":"c","en":"I haven’t eaten dinner yet.","jp":"まだ夕食を食べていません。"},{"id":"d","en":"I haven’t taken a bath yet.","jp":"まだお風呂に入っていません。"}],"correct":"a","image":"/assets/questions/visual/july-26-05-dinner-before-call.webp","imageAlt":"Dinner was finished before a phone call arrived.","visualAssetId":"july-26-05"}'::jsonb, false, 1),
    ('july-27', 'july-27-draft-choice-1', 0, 'Understand', 'mcq', '{"id":"july-27-draft-choice-1","format":"mcq","type":"mcq","section":"Understand","topic":"spill","isOriginal":false,"hint":"Focus on the spill meaning. Look for the sentence that expresses “シャツにコーヒーをこぼしました。”.","hintJa":"「シャツにコーヒーをこぼしました。」を表す英文と、spillの形に注目しましょう。","explanation":"“I spilled coffee on my shirt.” is the sentence that means “シャツにコーヒーをこぼしました。”. Check the complete meaning before choosing.","explanationJa":"「I spilled coffee on my shirt.」が「シャツにコーヒーをこぼしました。」を表す英文です。単語一つではなく文全体の意味で選びましょう。","prompt":"Choose the English sentence that means: シャツにコーヒーをこぼしました。","promptJa":"「シャツにコーヒーをこぼしました。」に合う英文を選んでください。","choices":[{"id":"a","en":"I spilled coffee on my shirt.","jp":"シャツにコーヒーをこぼしました。"},{"id":"b","en":"She poured sauce over the pasta.","jp":"彼女はパスタにソースをかけました。"},{"id":"c","en":"This dessert has a sophisticated flavor.","jp":"このデザートは洗練された味です。"},{"id":"d","en":"I had eaten before he arrived.","jp":"彼が着く前に食べていました。"}],"correct":"a"}'::jsonb, false, 1),
    ('july-27', 'july-27-draft-choice-2', 1, 'Understand', 'mcq', '{"id":"july-27-draft-choice-2","format":"mcq","type":"mcq","section":"Understand","topic":"pour","isOriginal":false,"hint":"Focus on the pour meaning. Look for the sentence that expresses “彼女はパスタにソースをかけました。”.","hintJa":"「彼女はパスタにソースをかけました。」を表す英文と、pourの形に注目しましょう。","explanation":"“She poured sauce over the pasta.” is the sentence that means “彼女はパスタにソースをかけました。”. Check the complete meaning before choosing.","explanationJa":"「She poured sauce over the pasta.」が「彼女はパスタにソースをかけました。」を表す英文です。単語一つではなく文全体の意味で選びましょう。","prompt":"Choose the English sentence that means: 彼女はパスタにソースをかけました。","promptJa":"「彼女はパスタにソースをかけました。」に合う英文を選んでください。","choices":[{"id":"a","en":"She poured sauce over the pasta.","jp":"彼女はパスタにソースをかけました。"},{"id":"b","en":"He splashed water on me.","jp":"彼は私に水をバシャッとかけました。"},{"id":"c","en":"He plays tennis every week.","jp":"彼は毎週テニスをします。"},{"id":"d","en":"I used to live here.","jp":"昔はここに住んでいました。"}],"correct":"a"}'::jsonb, false, 1),
    ('july-27', 'july-27-draft-choice-3', 2, 'Understand', 'mcq', '{"id":"july-27-draft-choice-3","format":"mcq","type":"mcq","section":"Understand","topic":"splash","isOriginal":false,"hint":"Focus on the splash meaning. Look for the sentence that expresses “彼は私に水をバシャッとかけました。”.","hintJa":"「彼は私に水をバシャッとかけました。」を表す英文と、splashの形に注目しましょう。","explanation":"“He splashed water on me.” is the sentence that means “彼は私に水をバシャッとかけました。”. Check the complete meaning before choosing.","explanationJa":"「He splashed water on me.」が「彼は私に水をバシャッとかけました。」を表す英文です。単語一つではなく文全体の意味で選びましょう。","prompt":"Choose the English sentence that means: 彼は私に水をバシャッとかけました。","promptJa":"「彼は私に水をバシャッとかけました。」に合う英文を選んでください。","choices":[{"id":"a","en":"He splashed water on me.","jp":"彼は私に水をバシャッとかけました。"},{"id":"b","en":"Coffee can be an acquired taste.","jp":"コーヒーは慣れると好きになる味です。"},{"id":"c","en":"I went to Malaysia last year.","jp":"去年マレーシアに行きました。"},{"id":"d","en":"I wish I had been invited.","jp":"招待されていたらよかった。"}],"correct":"a"}'::jsonb, false, 1),
    ('july-27', 'july-27-draft-choice-4', 3, 'Understand', 'mcq', '{"id":"july-27-draft-choice-4","format":"mcq","type":"mcq","section":"Understand","topic":"taste","isOriginal":false,"hint":"Focus on the taste meaning. Look for the sentence that expresses “コーヒーは慣れると好きになる味です。”.","hintJa":"「コーヒーは慣れると好きになる味です。」を表す英文と、tasteの形に注目しましょう。","explanation":"“Coffee can be an acquired taste.” is the sentence that means “コーヒーは慣れると好きになる味です。”. Check the complete meaning before choosing.","explanationJa":"「Coffee can be an acquired taste.」が「コーヒーは慣れると好きになる味です。」を表す英文です。単語一つではなく文全体の意味で選びましょう。","prompt":"Choose the English sentence that means: コーヒーは慣れると好きになる味です。","promptJa":"「コーヒーは慣れると好きになる味です。」に合う英文を選んでください。","choices":[{"id":"a","en":"Coffee can be an acquired taste.","jp":"コーヒーは慣れると好きになる味です。"},{"id":"b","en":"This dessert has a sophisticated flavor.","jp":"このデザートは洗練された味です。"},{"id":"c","en":"I have been to Malaysia.","jp":"マレーシアへ行ったことがあります。"},{"id":"d","en":"Don’t spill the beans.","jp":"秘密をばらさないで。"}],"correct":"a"}'::jsonb, false, 1),
    ('july-27', 'july-27-draft-true-false-1', 4, 'Understand', 'truefalse', '{"id":"july-27-draft-true-false-1","format":"truefalse","type":"truefalse","section":"Understand","topic":"taste","isOriginal":false,"hint":"Focus on the taste meaning. Look for the sentence that expresses “このデザートは洗練された味です。”.","hintJa":"「このデザートは洗練された味です。」を表す英文と、tasteの形に注目しましょう。","explanation":"True. “This dessert has a sophisticated flavor.” means “このデザートは洗練された味です。”.","explanationJa":"正解はTrueです。「This dessert has a sophisticated flavor.」は「このデザートは洗練された味です。」という意味です。","prompt":"“This dessert has a sophisticated flavor.” means “このデザートは洗練された味です。”.","promptJa":"「This dessert has a sophisticated flavor.」は「このデザートは洗練された味です。」という意味です。","correct":true}'::jsonb, false, 1),
    ('july-27', 'july-27-draft-true-false-2', 5, 'Understand', 'truefalse', '{"id":"july-27-draft-true-false-2","format":"truefalse","type":"truefalse","section":"Understand","topic":"present","isOriginal":false,"hint":"Focus on the present meaning. Look for the sentence that expresses “彼は毎週テニスをします。”.","hintJa":"「彼は毎週テニスをします。」を表す英文と、presentの形に注目しましょう。","explanation":"False. “He plays tennis every week.” means “彼は毎週テニスをします。”, not “去年マレーシアに行きました。”.","explanationJa":"正解はFalseです。「He plays tennis every week.」は「彼は毎週テニスをします。」であり、「去年マレーシアに行きました。」ではありません。","prompt":"“He plays tennis every week.” means “去年マレーシアに行きました。”.","promptJa":"「He plays tennis every week.」は「去年マレーシアに行きました。」という意味です。","correct":false}'::jsonb, false, 1),
