    ('july-27', 'july-27-draft-matching', 10, 'Build It', 'matching', '{"id":"july-27-draft-matching","format":"matching","type":"matching","section":"Build It","topic":"spill","isOriginal":false,"hint":"Focus on the spill meaning. Look for the sentence that expresses “シャツにコーヒーをこぼしました。”.","hintJa":"「シャツにコーヒーをこぼしました。」を表す英文と、spillの形に注目しましょう。","explanation":"Each English phrase has exactly one Japanese meaning. Match the whole message rather than isolated words.","explanationJa":"各英文に対応する日本語は一つです。単語だけではなく、表現全体の意味で組み合わせましょう。","prompt":"Match the English and Japanese.","promptJa":"英語と日本語を組み合わせてください。","pairs":[{"en":"I spilled coffee on my shirt.","jp":"シャツにコーヒーをこぼしました。","cat":"spill"},{"en":"She poured sauce over the pasta.","jp":"彼女はパスタにソースをかけました。","cat":"pour"},{"en":"He splashed water on me.","jp":"彼は私に水をバシャッとかけました。","cat":"splash"},{"en":"Coffee can be an acquired taste.","jp":"コーヒーは慣れると好きになる味です。","cat":"taste"},{"en":"This dessert has a sophisticated flavor.","jp":"このデザートは洗練された味です。","cat":"taste"},{"en":"He plays tennis every week.","jp":"彼は毎週テニスをします。","cat":"present"}]}'::jsonb, false, 6),
